WEBVTT

00:15.015 --> 00:17.016
[theme music playing]

00:56.556 --> 01:00.977
LOVE NEXT DOOR

01:03.313 --> 01:05.523
For our summer vacation this year,

01:06.024 --> 01:07.484
how about we try Alaska?

01:08.610 --> 01:09.611
I've always wanted to go.

01:10.445 --> 01:11.488
Well, I don't know.

01:11.571 --> 01:12.530
[groans softly]

01:13.656 --> 01:15.450
Then…

01:17.077 --> 01:18.953
Want to go hiking
at Yosemite National Park?

01:19.954 --> 01:21.164
Not really.

01:21.247 --> 01:23.917
Really? Then…

01:24.000 --> 01:24.918
New York?

01:25.001 --> 01:27.170
We can see shows and go to art museums.

01:27.670 --> 01:29.756
-Doesn't that sound nice?
-Not really.

01:29.839 --> 01:32.509
Forget it. Don't go.
We won't go anywhere then.

01:34.344 --> 01:36.721
I mean, we're both always so busy.

01:36.805 --> 01:40.850
So I wanted to at least spend
a proper summer vacation with you. Okay?

01:41.518 --> 01:44.854
But I was the only one excited
and had my hopes up for nothing.

01:50.485 --> 01:51.569
-Open it.
-What is it?

01:52.153 --> 01:53.613
You'll know once you open it.

02:03.289 --> 02:05.208
You haven't been to Korea in a while.

02:05.917 --> 02:07.418
Don't you miss your mom?

02:07.502 --> 02:08.711
[pleasant music playing]

02:08.795 --> 02:09.838
[exclaims softly]

02:10.922 --> 02:12.382
[Hyeon-jun] Are you going to cry?

02:12.465 --> 02:14.425
There are two tickets. I'm going too.

02:15.176 --> 02:16.136
Hyeon-jun.

02:16.219 --> 02:19.264
I think there's still something left
in the envelope.

02:28.523 --> 02:29.649
[Seok-ryu] What?

02:29.732 --> 02:30.984
[laughs]

02:37.782 --> 02:39.075
-[chuckles]
-[Seok-ryu exclaims]

02:40.118 --> 02:44.289
I didn't think I was going to
ask you this in my pajamas.

02:44.372 --> 02:45.707
[Seok-ryu laughs]

02:47.625 --> 02:49.460
Ever impatient and quick-tempered,
Seok-ryu…

02:49.544 --> 02:50.545
[exclaims]

02:52.714 --> 02:53.965
-[Seok-ryu chuckles]
-Will you…

02:55.508 --> 02:56.926
[chuckles softly]

02:57.010 --> 02:58.511
Will you marry me?

03:01.472 --> 03:02.682
Yes.

03:04.100 --> 03:06.728
I wanted to do this
somewhere nice on a special day.

03:09.606 --> 03:11.399
This moment right now is perfect.

03:11.482 --> 03:13.860
How could it get any better than this?

03:18.114 --> 03:18.948
[music fades]

03:19.532 --> 03:20.575
[phone vibrating]

03:22.035 --> 03:24.287
[female doctor] I'm afraid
it's stomach cancer.

03:24.370 --> 03:26.623
It appears to be early-stage,

03:26.706 --> 03:30.793
but the exact stage
can only be determined after surgery.

03:30.877 --> 03:33.671
We'll need to arrange an operation
for you as soon as possible…

03:33.755 --> 03:37.133
[voice fades] …and then discuss
treatment options post-surgery.

03:37.216 --> 03:40.053
But first, we'll need to run
some tests and biopsies.

03:40.136 --> 03:42.138
You need to make
an appointment with a clinic…

03:45.391 --> 03:47.060
[melancholy music playing]

03:47.977 --> 03:50.688
[footsteps]

03:51.648 --> 03:53.316
[Seok-ryu] I didn't get enough sleep.

03:54.400 --> 03:56.903
I had irregular meals.

03:58.071 --> 04:01.324
I was overexposed to stress.

04:04.160 --> 04:06.537
I was trying to figure out
why I got cancer

04:06.621 --> 04:08.790
when I suddenly looked out the window.

04:09.791 --> 04:12.043
The sky was so clear.

04:13.670 --> 04:15.255
I was 30 years old.

04:17.632 --> 04:23.263
DARKNESS IN LIFE

04:26.391 --> 04:29.352
[line ringing]

04:29.435 --> 04:30.687
Hey, Mo-eum. It's me.

04:31.229 --> 04:33.856
Tell me all the hospitals
in the area with an ER.

04:34.691 --> 04:35.525
[phone vibrating]

04:35.608 --> 04:36.609
CHOISSEUNG

04:38.319 --> 04:40.071
[footsteps approaching]

04:40.154 --> 04:42.073
[doctor] Do you feel dizzy or nauseous?

04:42.156 --> 04:43.741
No, I'm fine.

04:45.535 --> 04:48.538
This was Jeongheon University Hospital?

04:48.621 --> 04:50.123
You didn't know?

04:50.206 --> 04:52.333
Things were so frantic earlier.

04:52.417 --> 04:56.379
Is Professor Choi Gyeong-jong
here right now by any chance?

04:56.462 --> 04:57.964
He's off today.

04:58.047 --> 04:59.590
Do you know the professor?

04:59.674 --> 05:00.675
No.

05:00.758 --> 05:03.011
I saw him on TV.
You know how famous he is.

05:03.094 --> 05:06.222
I'm fine now, so I'll get going.

05:06.306 --> 05:08.641
Wait. You have to hear your test results.

05:09.225 --> 05:10.226
Okay.

05:10.852 --> 05:11.936
[doctor] Well…

05:12.562 --> 05:13.563
[inaudible conversation]

05:13.646 --> 05:15.148
[mysterious music playing]

05:19.027 --> 05:19.944
[car door closes]

05:20.903 --> 05:22.030
[Hyeon-jun] Seok-ryu.

05:24.741 --> 05:25.908
[Seok-ryu] Hyeon-jun.

05:25.992 --> 05:27.452
Why are you still here?

05:27.535 --> 05:29.245
How could I have left you here?

05:29.829 --> 05:32.206
Did you get examined?
What did the doctor say?

05:33.458 --> 05:35.793
Did a recurrence…

05:38.087 --> 05:39.172
[tires screech]

05:42.050 --> 05:43.301
Seok-ryu!

05:44.510 --> 05:45.428
Choisseung.

05:45.928 --> 05:48.056
Are you okay?
Does your stomach still hurt?

05:48.139 --> 05:49.140
No.

05:49.932 --> 05:51.726
Why did it hurt? What was wrong?

05:51.809 --> 05:53.394
Well, you know…

05:53.478 --> 05:56.522
How did you know I was here?
Did someone tell you?

05:56.606 --> 05:58.524
Look, no one told me.

05:58.608 --> 06:00.068
So what did they say?

06:00.151 --> 06:02.653
They said I was fine.
Why are you shouting?

06:02.737 --> 06:03.821
I can hear you, okay?

06:04.781 --> 06:08.242
Excuse me? I'm standing here too.
You could acknowledge me.

06:08.326 --> 06:09.452
Oh.

06:09.535 --> 06:10.703
You were here?

06:11.579 --> 06:13.081
I wasn't concerned with you.

06:13.164 --> 06:14.123
[Hyeon-jun exhales]

06:15.208 --> 06:17.085
Let's go. I'll take you home.

06:17.168 --> 06:18.336
Come with me.

06:18.419 --> 06:21.714
I don't care who I go with.
Let's just go now.

06:21.798 --> 06:24.133
[Hyeon-jun] You really know
how to interfere.

06:24.217 --> 06:26.344
But don't cross the line.

06:26.427 --> 06:28.346
This is something between me and her.

06:29.472 --> 06:30.306
What?

06:31.057 --> 06:33.059
Hyeon-jun, I'll go home with Choisseung.

06:33.601 --> 06:35.853
-What?
-It's in the same direction.

06:36.354 --> 06:37.480
Thanks for today.

06:39.107 --> 06:39.941
[exhales]

06:43.694 --> 06:44.529
[exhales]

06:45.113 --> 06:46.572
Call me when you get there.

06:46.656 --> 06:47.532
I'll wait.

06:47.615 --> 06:48.699
Don't wait.

06:48.783 --> 06:50.243
I'm putting her to bed early.

06:50.326 --> 06:52.578
To me, Seok-ryu isn't some child.

06:53.079 --> 06:53.913
She's a woman.

06:54.956 --> 06:56.249
[melancholy music playing]

06:57.416 --> 06:58.251
Let's go.

07:12.348 --> 07:13.808
[car accelerating]

07:28.823 --> 07:30.116
It's stomach cancer?

07:35.955 --> 07:37.331
[voice shaking] What do I do now?

07:42.253 --> 07:43.713
I'm so scared.

07:45.756 --> 07:48.050
No, there's no need to be scared.

07:48.968 --> 07:50.011
I'll fix it for you.

07:50.470 --> 07:52.263
I'll do what I can to help cure you.

07:53.055 --> 07:55.183
Medical technology
has improved these days.

07:55.266 --> 07:57.018
You'll be fine
with early detection.

07:57.101 --> 07:59.937
I have a friend who works
at that hospital.

08:00.021 --> 08:01.355
I'll call him right now.

08:01.898 --> 08:03.733
I'll see if we can move up your surgery.

08:04.859 --> 08:07.195
Okay. Starting tomorrow,

08:07.278 --> 08:09.197
-take a sick leave.
-[Seok-ryu sniffles]

08:09.280 --> 08:11.908
-I'll apply for a leave of absence too.
-You too?

08:14.202 --> 08:17.121
You're on an important case right now.
You can't do that.

08:17.205 --> 08:18.581
Nothing's more important than you.

08:19.624 --> 08:20.917
Don't worry.

08:21.584 --> 08:23.044
I'll stay by your side.

08:30.593 --> 08:32.386
Hey, just wait one second.

08:44.315 --> 08:45.816
You want me to get out?

08:46.400 --> 08:47.527
Yeah.

08:52.406 --> 08:55.243
What's going on?
Why are you doing this?

08:55.326 --> 08:56.452
I'm just being polite.

08:57.286 --> 09:00.665
If a guy does something
like this for you, just accept it.

09:00.748 --> 09:02.959
Don't do it. It's weird.

09:03.793 --> 09:05.670
You'd always treat me like a servant.

09:05.753 --> 09:07.755
Now, this princess treatment
is bewildering me.

09:07.838 --> 09:09.840
It looked like Hyeon-jun
treated you this way.

09:15.888 --> 09:17.598
Never mind. Go in.

09:47.503 --> 09:48.921
[Hyeon-jun] Don't you think

09:49.005 --> 09:50.965
you should tell your parents back home?

09:51.048 --> 09:52.466
[line ringing]

09:52.550 --> 09:54.719
-[humming]
-[phone ringing]

09:54.802 --> 09:56.095
♪ What's love ♪

09:56.178 --> 09:57.013
[gasps]

10:00.349 --> 10:01.642
Hey, you brat!

10:01.726 --> 10:04.812
Why is it so hard to reach you?
I thought something happened.

10:04.895 --> 10:07.940
Nothing happened. What are you up to?

10:08.024 --> 10:09.275
What perfect timing.

10:09.358 --> 10:11.235
I'm making kimchi for you.

10:11.319 --> 10:13.529
Forget it. Don't send it.

10:13.613 --> 10:15.656
I can just buy it here if I need to.

10:15.740 --> 10:18.034
It's from another country,
so it won't taste the same.

10:18.117 --> 10:20.578
I got cabbages from Gangwon-do.
They're so good.

10:20.661 --> 10:22.538
No, I said don't send it.

10:22.622 --> 10:25.207
I told you not to last time,
but you sent it anyway.

10:26.208 --> 10:27.793
It leaked out of the box.

10:27.877 --> 10:29.587
Do you know how embarrassed I was?

10:29.670 --> 10:32.340
It's because I was greedy.
I tried to fill it to the top.

10:32.423 --> 10:33.799
I'll be more careful this time.

10:33.883 --> 10:35.301
No, I don't want it.

10:35.384 --> 10:36.802
I told you I don't need it.

10:36.886 --> 10:38.971
Why won't you listen to me?

10:39.055 --> 10:41.223
Listen to me when I tell you something!

10:42.183 --> 10:44.685
Then, eat as much as you want
when you come here.

10:44.769 --> 10:45.728
When's your flight?

10:46.479 --> 10:47.647
I can't go.

10:48.939 --> 10:50.650
[slow music playing]

10:50.733 --> 10:52.568
I won't be able to
call for a while either.

10:52.652 --> 10:55.071
Why? Are you really busy?

10:55.154 --> 10:57.907
Yeah, I started a new project.

10:58.407 --> 10:59.408
It's very important.

10:59.492 --> 11:00.451
Oh.

11:00.951 --> 11:01.994
Okay, I get it.

11:02.078 --> 11:04.664
You're doing important work.
I shouldn't bother you.

11:04.747 --> 11:05.748
Even if you have no time,

11:05.831 --> 11:08.584
don't skip meals, drink a lot of water,
and get a lot of sleep.

11:08.668 --> 11:10.336
Call me more often too.

11:11.337 --> 11:14.298
Okay. I think…

11:15.257 --> 11:17.468
I think I'm getting a call from work. Bye.

11:17.551 --> 11:18.803
-Okay…
-[line disconnects]

11:21.972 --> 11:23.724
[clicks tongue] That brat.

11:26.394 --> 11:27.269
[sighs]

11:30.314 --> 11:31.774
[sobbing]

11:35.361 --> 11:38.072
[sobbing] It's okay, Seok-ryu.
It's not a big deal.

11:38.614 --> 11:42.284
[sniffles] I'll get better.
I'll tell them after I get better.

11:42.910 --> 11:45.496
It's not a big deal. It's nothing.

11:48.749 --> 11:49.834
[sobbing]

11:59.427 --> 12:01.303
[faint footsteps]

12:02.388 --> 12:03.222
[groans softly]

12:05.766 --> 12:06.851
[exhales]

12:09.270 --> 12:10.229
[sighs]

12:12.148 --> 12:14.483
[pinging]

12:19.363 --> 12:20.322
-[pings]
-[grunts]

12:22.908 --> 12:25.119
Hyeon-jun, hold me up.

12:25.202 --> 12:26.704
[Hyeon-jun] You can lean on me.

12:29.999 --> 12:32.209
To me, Seok-ryu isn't some child.

12:32.710 --> 12:33.544
She's a woman.

12:33.627 --> 12:34.879
-[thuds]
-[grunts]

12:34.962 --> 12:36.380
[Mo-eum clapping]

12:36.464 --> 12:39.425
Nice batting stance.
Your timing's perfect too.

12:40.050 --> 12:41.802
-Hey.
-[Mo-eum] "Hey"?

12:41.886 --> 12:46.515
You're having fun hitting balls alone
after giving me a scare like that?

12:46.599 --> 12:49.351
You can join if you want.
You need some cash?

12:49.435 --> 12:50.936
[Mo-eum] I have money too, you fool.

12:51.020 --> 12:52.271
It's been a while.

12:53.105 --> 12:56.358
Goodness, how about we loosen up a bit?

12:56.942 --> 12:57.860
-[thuds]
-[grunts]

12:58.986 --> 13:00.571
[Mo-eum] Oh. Wow.

13:00.654 --> 13:02.907
No matter how I think about it,
it's amazing.

13:03.407 --> 13:06.535
You don't look like someone
who'd be good at sports.

13:06.619 --> 13:08.329
If you're here to pick a fight, save it.

13:09.079 --> 13:10.206
I'm not in the mood.

13:10.289 --> 13:13.042
I'm sure you aren't.

13:13.125 --> 13:14.210
What's wrong?

13:15.085 --> 13:16.462
Is it Seok-ryu again?

13:17.755 --> 13:18.672
[laughing]

13:19.256 --> 13:21.091
-[sighs wearily]
-[Mo-eum laughing]

13:21.175 --> 13:22.218
[exhales]

13:22.927 --> 13:27.181
So she went to the hospital
with that punk instead of you?

13:27.264 --> 13:28.974
[pop song playing in the background]

13:29.058 --> 13:30.059
Wow.

13:30.142 --> 13:32.520
I guess I did beam you with a fastball.

13:33.521 --> 13:35.773
-Is this fun for you?
-A little.

13:36.398 --> 13:37.775
[clears throat] So?

13:37.858 --> 13:39.443
Did you ask her?

13:39.944 --> 13:42.530
Why did she choose him at that moment?

13:42.613 --> 13:43.614
[sighs]

13:43.697 --> 13:45.032
No.

13:45.115 --> 13:46.992
Jeez, you're so frustrating and dumb.

13:47.576 --> 13:50.037
You still haven't fixed
that chronic habit.

13:51.121 --> 13:53.916
Do I need to step up to the plate?

13:53.999 --> 13:55.417
Forget it.

13:55.501 --> 13:56.335
You're right.

13:56.877 --> 13:59.380
Whether you hit a home run
or strike out, it's up to you.

14:00.965 --> 14:03.884
Then, say something
so I can at least cheer you on.

14:04.510 --> 14:05.636
Tell me your feelings.

14:06.428 --> 14:08.597
How are you feeling right now?

14:10.641 --> 14:11.517
I feel like crap.

14:12.977 --> 14:14.436
I feel jealous too.

14:16.855 --> 14:17.982
I told Seok-ryu

14:18.566 --> 14:20.776
I wouldn't ask
about why her engagement was called off.

14:21.860 --> 14:23.112
And I told him

14:24.029 --> 14:27.575
I wasn't curious
since things were over between them.

14:27.658 --> 14:29.118
I pretended not to care.

14:30.953 --> 14:32.371
But I want to ask so badly.

14:33.831 --> 14:35.416
I'm so curious it's driving me crazy.

14:37.585 --> 14:40.462
There's a gap
between Seok-ryu and me.

14:41.755 --> 14:43.424
And Hyeon-jun

14:44.425 --> 14:46.969
is inside of it
with a part of her I don't know.

14:48.470 --> 14:51.056
It's… How can I explain it?

14:52.850 --> 14:54.560
It makes me angry.

14:55.644 --> 14:58.105
Think about all the time
you've been together for.

14:58.939 --> 15:00.774
If they're American history,

15:00.858 --> 15:03.527
you two are like
the four great ancient civilizations.

15:03.611 --> 15:06.238
You're like Egypt and Mesopotamia.

15:06.822 --> 15:09.575
So don't be scared. Don't shrink back.

15:11.243 --> 15:12.328
[amusing music playing]

15:12.411 --> 15:13.495
I didn't.

15:13.579 --> 15:17.541
No, you've shrunk
and wrinkled up a lot lately.

15:17.625 --> 15:18.459
You've aged too.

15:19.084 --> 15:20.544
How? Really?

15:21.587 --> 15:24.381
What's the big deal about having a crush?

15:28.218 --> 15:29.553
Hey.

15:30.554 --> 15:33.682
Does your heart start to beat too?

15:33.766 --> 15:36.226
How can someone live
if their heart doesn't beat?

15:36.310 --> 15:38.270
That's not what I meant.

15:39.355 --> 15:42.608
So when a person likes another person,

15:43.651 --> 15:47.529
does your heart beat faster?

15:48.197 --> 15:49.323
Of course.

15:50.491 --> 15:52.117
It races when we're together.

15:53.661 --> 15:55.245
It races when she's with someone else.

15:55.329 --> 15:58.999
Like the fast, rumbling beat
of Korean traditional drums?

15:59.083 --> 16:01.377
What? What are you rambling about?

16:01.460 --> 16:02.920
Forget I said anything.

16:04.505 --> 16:05.714
Never mind.

16:05.798 --> 16:08.467
So how's Seok-ryu? Is she okay?

16:08.550 --> 16:10.511
[exhales] I don't know.

16:11.011 --> 16:12.346
[exclaims]

16:12.429 --> 16:14.932
That brat's been picking
at her food a lot lately.

16:15.015 --> 16:16.266
Is she getting old too?

16:16.767 --> 16:18.978
She could eat dirt and be fine back then.

16:19.687 --> 16:21.021
[sighs audibly]

16:21.105 --> 16:22.564
[Mo-eum] Seriously.

16:27.736 --> 16:28.570
[Seok-ryu exhales]

16:30.280 --> 16:31.115
HYEON-JUN

16:31.198 --> 16:32.574
Make sure to take your medicine.

16:39.999 --> 16:41.583
[pills rattling]

16:45.587 --> 16:47.840
I'm so sick of this.

16:48.674 --> 16:49.675
[mellow music playing]

16:49.758 --> 16:50.968
[closes drawer]

16:55.931 --> 16:56.765
[exhales]

16:58.058 --> 16:59.601
It's late. Go to bed.

17:02.980 --> 17:03.981
[chuckles softly]

17:05.607 --> 17:06.984
Good night, Seok-ryu.

17:17.327 --> 17:21.790
[Seok-ryu] After I got sick,
I'd lie in bed every night and think.

17:22.958 --> 17:24.835
I'd think, "Why is it called cancer?"

17:26.754 --> 17:29.173
Names are important for everything.

17:29.256 --> 17:31.300
"Cancer" sounds so dark and scary.

17:32.760 --> 17:35.179
"Flower." "Moon." "Star."

17:36.221 --> 17:40.100
It would've been better if it had
a brighter and more cheerful name.

17:48.817 --> 17:49.860
[birds chirping]

17:55.324 --> 17:57.701
[door opens, closes]

17:57.785 --> 17:59.036
He has some nerve.

18:00.120 --> 18:01.663
[door opens]

18:02.289 --> 18:03.624
-Dad, I--
-I'm off.

18:03.707 --> 18:05.292
-Okay, have a good day.
-[Geun-sik] Bye.

18:05.375 --> 18:06.752
[door opens]

18:06.835 --> 18:08.295
-[Mi-suk sighs]
-[door closes]

18:08.378 --> 18:11.298
I won't stop you
from taking cooking classes.

18:13.092 --> 18:14.843
Nothing bad can come from learning.

18:14.927 --> 18:16.470
It'll be beneficial to you.

18:17.179 --> 18:19.556
-Really?
-[Mi-suk] Of course. [exclaims]

18:19.640 --> 18:22.101
It's something we do to survive.
It's a great hobby.

18:23.102 --> 18:25.312
Learn and use those skills
when you get married.

18:25.938 --> 18:28.857
Also, I thought about it.

18:28.941 --> 18:31.193
You don't have to go
to the US if you don't want to.

18:31.276 --> 18:33.779
But instead, get a job here.

18:33.862 --> 18:36.532
You could easily join a major company
with your background.

18:36.615 --> 18:37.574
Mom.

18:37.658 --> 18:39.409
You're allowed to wander for a bit.

18:40.160 --> 18:43.497
But you have all that experience.
Think of your future.

18:43.580 --> 18:45.415
I'll decide my future.

18:46.500 --> 18:48.085
And that's cooking.

18:48.168 --> 18:49.336
Don't be ridiculous.

18:49.419 --> 18:51.338
Your father and I won't ever allow it.

18:51.421 --> 18:53.674
What parent would stand by
and let their child stray?

18:53.757 --> 18:55.551
I'm not straying. I'm on the right path.

18:56.218 --> 18:58.804
I didn't even know
what my path was up until now.

18:58.887 --> 19:01.890
I've just been running like crazy,
but I finally found direction.

19:01.974 --> 19:05.227
It's a path full of thorns.
You'll get stuck in the mud!

19:05.310 --> 19:07.521
Stop wasting time
and focus on getting a job.

19:08.397 --> 19:09.231
[door opens]

19:09.314 --> 19:11.441
My advice isn't worth
listening to anymore?

19:11.942 --> 19:14.695
I worked so hard to raise you.
You think you did it on your own?

19:21.535 --> 19:22.369
[door slams]

19:22.452 --> 19:23.912
What took you so long?

19:23.996 --> 19:25.289
I was starving to death.

19:25.372 --> 19:28.083
What? Did we have a prior engagement
that I don't know about?

19:28.709 --> 19:31.086
-Did you fight with your mom again?
-Mind your own business.

19:31.170 --> 19:32.546
Let's get something to eat.

19:34.673 --> 19:35.716
Like what?

19:37.050 --> 19:40.053
Is this really all you could pick to eat?

19:40.137 --> 19:43.515
You looked beat up like this porridge.
That's why I picked it. What's wrong?

19:43.599 --> 19:45.392
-You little…
-[stomach growling]

19:45.475 --> 19:46.602
[chuckles softly]

19:46.685 --> 19:48.270
Just eat. Try it first.

19:48.353 --> 19:49.688
[quirky music playing]

19:49.771 --> 19:52.733
I'm mad I have to spend
a precious meal eating soft food.

19:58.947 --> 19:59.948
What is this?

20:00.657 --> 20:02.326
-Why is it good?
-Right?

20:03.368 --> 20:04.912
This place is good.

20:04.995 --> 20:06.955
I won't bring you to just any place.

20:07.623 --> 20:09.499
What are you talking about?
Hurry up and eat.

20:10.083 --> 20:10.959
Okay.

20:28.310 --> 20:29.353
Mmm.

20:36.318 --> 20:37.486
That was so good.

20:38.654 --> 20:42.324
Remember when you were complaining?
I thought you'd eat the bowl too.

20:42.407 --> 20:44.701
Of course. I could eat steel bars too.

20:44.785 --> 20:45.994
This bowl is nothing.

20:49.873 --> 20:51.750
What? Are you feeling sick again?

20:52.251 --> 20:55.295
Since it was a bit bland,
I'm craving tteokbokki now.

20:55.963 --> 20:57.798
Do you even have room
after eating all that?

20:57.881 --> 20:59.383
I can make room.

21:00.717 --> 21:02.302
I'm going to the restroom.

21:06.098 --> 21:08.141
Ma'am, do you have any toilet paper?

21:08.225 --> 21:10.394
[employee] No,
take some from the roll here.

21:14.356 --> 21:16.441
[bird chirping]

21:16.525 --> 21:18.944
Yeah, you have to make room for more.

21:20.696 --> 21:22.698
[sighs] I must be crazy about her.

21:23.490 --> 21:24.491
[chuckles softly]

21:27.619 --> 21:28.704
[exhales]

21:29.871 --> 21:31.581
[solemn music playing]

21:31.665 --> 21:32.708
[groans weakly]

21:34.084 --> 21:35.961
[exhales] Did I eat too quickly?

21:36.044 --> 21:37.170
[breathes weakly]

21:37.254 --> 21:39.006
I'm getting dumping syndrome again.

21:39.089 --> 21:40.007
[inhales]

21:41.383 --> 21:42.342
[exhales]

21:44.011 --> 21:45.762
[dance music playing in the background]

21:49.182 --> 21:51.685
[Dong-jin] Wow, he has a great body.

21:52.185 --> 21:53.103
[gasps]

21:53.186 --> 21:54.479
Look at his back.

21:55.689 --> 21:59.276
Wow, I heard you make hundreds
of thousands with just one ad.

21:59.860 --> 22:01.695
I wish I could get just one offer.

22:01.778 --> 22:03.196
[phone chimes]

22:05.407 --> 22:07.492
WE'D LIKE YOU TO HELP PROMOTE
OUR NEW PRODUCT

22:07.576 --> 22:08.660
[cash register dings]

22:10.120 --> 22:12.414
It's here! A life-changing opportunity!

22:13.081 --> 22:14.207
[chuckling]

22:15.417 --> 22:19.880
Just you wait, Seok-ryu.
I'll succeed. I'll show you.

22:22.257 --> 22:23.675
Thank you.

22:23.759 --> 22:25.927
This is my first promotion.
What do I need to do?

22:28.138 --> 22:29.681
[chuckles softly]

22:29.765 --> 22:31.058
How cute.

22:41.485 --> 22:43.070
What's this?

22:43.153 --> 22:45.655
Did we really not take
that many photos together?

22:46.281 --> 22:47.783
-[glass breaking]
-That scared me!

22:49.701 --> 22:51.119
What was that?

22:51.745 --> 22:52.913
What's going on?

22:53.955 --> 22:55.165
Goodness.

22:55.916 --> 22:56.750
[gasps]

22:57.667 --> 22:58.752
[breathing heavily]

23:00.170 --> 23:02.255
My goodness. How did this happen?

23:04.132 --> 23:05.383
[exclaims]

23:05.967 --> 23:07.094
[pleasant music playing]

23:11.640 --> 23:13.266
Are you okay? Were you hurt?

23:13.350 --> 23:14.935
No, I'm okay.

23:16.812 --> 23:19.106
The washing machine suddenly…

23:24.778 --> 23:26.780
It's dangerous,
so go and sit. I'll clean this.

23:27.447 --> 23:30.033
Yeah, okay.

23:32.077 --> 23:33.245
[vacuum humming]

23:33.328 --> 23:34.287
[vacuum stops]

23:37.499 --> 23:38.750
[Gyeong-jong groans]

23:44.714 --> 23:46.174
I'm finished cleaning.

23:46.758 --> 23:49.136
I vacuumed too,
but there still could be some shards.

23:49.219 --> 23:50.595
Don't walk around barefoot.

23:51.513 --> 23:52.931
As for the washing machine,

23:53.849 --> 23:55.142
I'll call for a repair tech.

23:56.268 --> 23:57.561
Wait.

24:01.982 --> 24:03.316
You're bleeding!

24:09.531 --> 24:11.241
[groaning]

24:14.119 --> 24:15.829
I said I could do it.

24:15.912 --> 24:17.080
I'll do it.

24:17.164 --> 24:20.041
Still, I'm a professor of ER medicine.

24:20.125 --> 24:21.209
[Hye-suk scoffs]

24:21.293 --> 24:23.837
I guess ER professors bleed
after stepping on glass too.

24:24.713 --> 24:25.881
[exclaims]

24:25.964 --> 24:27.215
-[chuckles softly]
-That stings.

24:27.299 --> 24:28.925
And he's a crybaby.

24:29.926 --> 24:30.886
[blows air]

24:30.969 --> 24:33.263
I get hurt like other people too.

24:33.346 --> 24:35.056
Pain receptors don't discriminate.

24:35.807 --> 24:37.642
-Pain receptors?
-[Gyeong-jong] Did you know?

24:37.726 --> 24:42.647
Pain receptors don't distinguish
between physical pain and emotional pain.

24:43.273 --> 24:46.776
Whether it's being cut by glass
or emotionally hurt,

24:46.860 --> 24:47.819
they react the same.

24:49.863 --> 24:50.739
Really?

24:53.033 --> 24:53.867
All done.

24:54.951 --> 24:57.120
Well, I'm just saying.

24:58.705 --> 24:59.539
I'll get going.

25:00.207 --> 25:01.374
[Hye-suk] Hey.

25:03.793 --> 25:05.212
Do you want some ramyeon?

25:05.295 --> 25:07.172
[pleasant music playing]

25:15.513 --> 25:16.348
[closes cupboard]

25:20.852 --> 25:21.978
Stop staring at me.

25:22.062 --> 25:23.188
Right!

25:25.398 --> 25:27.525
Does she have eyes
in the back of her head?

25:37.619 --> 25:38.703
[device beeping]

25:39.788 --> 25:40.622
[chuckles softly]

25:43.250 --> 25:44.542
[timer winding]

25:55.136 --> 25:56.054
[slurps]

26:00.600 --> 26:01.935
[slurping]

26:05.355 --> 26:07.774
It's good. The noodles are al dente.

26:07.857 --> 26:09.276
-It tastes just right.
-Yeah.

26:10.318 --> 26:11.987
Cooking ramyeon is a science.

26:12.654 --> 26:14.155
I just haven't tried,

26:14.239 --> 26:16.908
but as long as I know the recipe,
I can make anything.

26:19.119 --> 26:20.870
This reminds me of the past.

26:21.621 --> 26:24.124
We ate this often in my dorm near school.

26:24.207 --> 26:25.250
[chuckles softly]

26:26.042 --> 26:27.419
Do you remember?

26:28.211 --> 26:29.587
Back then,

26:30.380 --> 26:33.133
you threw up your ramyeon
after studying anatomy with cadavers.

26:34.551 --> 26:36.511
[chuckling] I never did that.

26:36.594 --> 26:40.223
You did. You looked so pale.
You were the one who looked like a corpse.

26:40.307 --> 26:41.683
What are you talking about?

26:41.766 --> 26:44.185
I was a promising young talent
from the start. [chuckles]

26:44.269 --> 26:45.812
[Hye-suk chuckles]

26:45.895 --> 26:48.189
Yeah, a promising talent indeed.

26:48.273 --> 26:51.276
I'd never seen anyone study
as well as you did.

26:54.571 --> 26:55.697
Why are you out here?

26:56.281 --> 26:57.699
Because we were done eating.

26:58.199 --> 26:59.951
-Here.
-Thank you.

27:00.493 --> 27:02.370
-Thanks for the meal.
-Take this too.

27:04.706 --> 27:07.250
What is this exciting black bag?

27:07.334 --> 27:08.918
Is it tteokbokki?

27:10.545 --> 27:12.172
[Seung-hyo] Take them as per your needs.

27:12.672 --> 27:14.257
What a bummer.

27:14.799 --> 27:16.051
I don't need this stuff.

27:16.134 --> 27:18.345
I have to get to work now.
Tomorrow's chicken porridge.

27:18.428 --> 27:20.555
-Who says I'll eat with you?
-Bye.

27:20.638 --> 27:21.973
[phone vibrating]

27:22.057 --> 27:24.684
[Seung-hyo] Hey, I'm on my way now. Okay.

27:26.936 --> 27:29.731
That fool bought so much. It's so heavy.

27:33.360 --> 27:34.235
[door closes]

27:35.945 --> 27:37.447
-[Myeong-u sighs]
-Don't move!

27:37.530 --> 27:40.825
What? What's the matter?
What's going on?

27:40.909 --> 27:41.951
[Seung-hyo] Oh.

27:42.035 --> 27:45.246
That milk!
Did you steal that from my fridge?

27:45.330 --> 27:47.207
-You did.
-[Myeong-u chuckles] Yeah.

27:47.290 --> 27:49.250
Right, I guess you could say that. Why?

27:49.918 --> 27:51.419
Just carefully put it down.

27:51.503 --> 27:52.754
-[Myeong-u] What?
-No, wait.

27:52.837 --> 27:54.422
Just give it to me.

27:54.506 --> 27:56.466
Seriously? It's just milk.
Don't be stingy--

27:56.549 --> 27:57.592
It's not just milk!

27:57.675 --> 27:59.928
My life depends on this milk.

28:00.011 --> 28:02.889
Hey, why do so many things
in your office depend on something?

28:02.972 --> 28:06.810
Last time, you said our company's success
depended on that tree… My gosh!

28:06.893 --> 28:07.852
What now?

28:07.936 --> 28:08.937
Our company.

28:10.021 --> 28:11.856
-What?
-Our company is withering.

28:16.361 --> 28:17.904
[doorbell chiming]

28:26.704 --> 28:27.705
We're not open yet--

28:27.789 --> 28:29.416
Hello.

28:29.499 --> 28:30.667
It's this.

28:31.209 --> 28:32.710
Can you save my tree?

28:32.794 --> 28:33.711
Oh.

28:34.295 --> 28:35.130
This tree?

28:35.839 --> 28:37.006
Yes.

28:37.090 --> 28:38.591
[shop owner] Okay.

28:42.095 --> 28:43.555
[pleasant music playing]

28:43.638 --> 28:44.639
[chuckles softly]

28:46.057 --> 28:47.809
I thought it was an emergency.

28:48.435 --> 28:50.019
You sounded so desperate to save it.

28:50.103 --> 28:53.982
It suddenly started to wither,
so I thought it was an emergency.

28:54.065 --> 28:56.943
I guess you don't talk to it often.

28:58.153 --> 28:59.154
Talk to it?

28:59.237 --> 29:01.614
We may not hear them,
but plants can speak too.

29:01.698 --> 29:03.616
They say they're tired or hungry.

29:05.368 --> 29:07.871
This one's saying it's too humid.

29:07.954 --> 29:09.914
This will stop it from bearing fruit.

29:10.498 --> 29:12.667
It can bear fruit?

29:12.751 --> 29:15.628
-Can it bloom flowers too?
-Of course. [chuckles softly]

29:17.130 --> 29:19.007
Our friend has a lot to do this year.

29:20.133 --> 29:21.426
[Seung-hyo] Then…

29:21.509 --> 29:24.387
What should I do to listen to my tree?

29:25.722 --> 29:28.266
So I was grilling
the dried pollock earlier.

29:29.726 --> 29:33.104
I think meat's better than fish.
I was craving pork belly so badly.

29:33.188 --> 29:34.272
[all laughing]

29:43.615 --> 29:44.657
Are you done?

29:45.492 --> 29:46.910
You looked so happy earlier.

29:48.411 --> 29:49.454
What?

29:51.331 --> 29:52.957
You were smiling so beautifully.

29:54.793 --> 29:57.420
It was like you returned
to your familiar usual self.

29:58.421 --> 30:01.257
What was my usual self like?

30:01.341 --> 30:03.092
You're brighter
than California sunshine.

30:03.676 --> 30:06.429
Bright, positive, and full of energy.

30:11.434 --> 30:12.352
Open it.

30:17.315 --> 30:19.317
-What is this?
-[envelope rustling]

30:21.194 --> 30:24.364
[Hyeon-jun] Remember the cooking school
I mentioned last time?

30:25.073 --> 30:27.033
I got these from a study abroad agency.

30:27.116 --> 30:28.910
If you're going to start this,

30:30.119 --> 30:32.914
I want you to take
a proper path so you won't fail.

30:37.168 --> 30:39.087
There's one more thing in there.

30:49.889 --> 30:51.599
[mellow music playing]

30:51.683 --> 30:53.309
-Is this…
-[Hyeon-jun] Yeah.

30:53.977 --> 30:55.311
It's the engagement ring

30:56.479 --> 30:57.564
that you left behind.

30:59.566 --> 31:02.360
Just like how you've begun to dream again,

31:03.236 --> 31:04.988
let's start over again too.

31:06.656 --> 31:08.408
I want to continue to support you.

31:09.534 --> 31:10.618
I want to be with you.

31:37.937 --> 31:39.522
Nice reflexes.

31:39.606 --> 31:41.566
That's what we former athletes
pride ourselves on.

31:43.318 --> 31:44.777
Is this for me?

31:44.861 --> 31:46.529
SSING-SSING BAR

31:48.823 --> 31:49.949
[clicks tongue, inhales]

31:50.033 --> 31:52.452
You should always split
and share this ice cream.

31:53.036 --> 31:53.870
I agree.

31:54.954 --> 31:56.789
[Seok-ryu] There are no stars
or moon tonight.

31:59.626 --> 32:01.377
[Mo-eum] Did you ask her?

32:01.461 --> 32:04.464
Why did she choose him at that moment?

32:06.591 --> 32:08.468
-About that night…
-He proposed to me.

32:10.219 --> 32:11.054
What?

32:11.721 --> 32:13.598
Hyeon-jun proposed to me.

32:20.438 --> 32:21.439
[exhales audibly]

32:22.023 --> 32:23.691
Wow, he must be a lunatic.

32:25.234 --> 32:27.028
I wanted to at least be respectful,

32:27.111 --> 32:28.488
he's really ticking me off.

32:29.739 --> 32:31.824
What on earth is he doing? It's too late.

32:32.533 --> 32:33.785
What if it isn't late?

32:36.204 --> 32:37.288
What?

32:38.873 --> 32:42.585
When he proposed for the second time,
I had this thought.

32:43.795 --> 32:45.338
"Maybe it's not too late."

32:47.590 --> 32:51.469
He keeps taking me back to the good times.

32:55.890 --> 32:57.642
It's like a breeze
blowing through my heart.

32:59.018 --> 33:01.020
And the book I once closed
is open again.

33:01.980 --> 33:04.023
I remember all of my forgotten memories.

33:05.566 --> 33:08.486
The osam bulgogi we ate when we first met.

33:09.320 --> 33:11.114
It was so good.

33:11.197 --> 33:12.281
Things like that.

33:16.703 --> 33:17.870
Even though I'm here?

33:19.914 --> 33:21.040
Yeah.

33:23.501 --> 33:24.377
Even though…

33:26.004 --> 33:27.171
I told you how I felt?

33:29.465 --> 33:30.758
Yeah.

33:34.303 --> 33:35.138
[exhales]

33:35.221 --> 33:36.639
[slow music playing]

33:38.182 --> 33:41.019
Is that why you went
to the hospital with him and not me?

33:41.602 --> 33:43.187
Yeah, it was like instinct.

33:43.813 --> 33:45.314
Usually,

33:45.398 --> 33:48.067
people become the most vulnerable
and honest when they're sick.

33:48.776 --> 33:50.903
I guess I subconsciously
wanted to lean on him.

33:52.488 --> 33:53.990
You can't lean on me?

33:55.992 --> 33:57.118
To me,

33:58.745 --> 34:00.121
you're still…

34:00.955 --> 34:03.875
a five-year-old kid crying
at the top of a jungle gym.

34:06.252 --> 34:08.504
A childhood friend
I can split ice cream with.

34:08.588 --> 34:10.506
The successful son of my mom's friend.

34:21.059 --> 34:22.268
[exhales]

34:22.351 --> 34:23.853
You're so cruel.

34:24.687 --> 34:25.521
[clicks tongue]

34:26.189 --> 34:27.565
How could you…

34:28.858 --> 34:31.027
How can you make it
so I can't say anything?

34:32.737 --> 34:34.655
I'm letting you know. You're mistaken.

34:37.617 --> 34:40.119
You don't like me. You imprinted on me.

34:41.204 --> 34:42.663
Did you know?

34:42.747 --> 34:44.207
A duckling mistakes

34:44.290 --> 34:47.418
the first thing it sees
for its mother and follows them around.

34:47.502 --> 34:49.128
-[sighs]
-[Seok-ryu] It's like that.

34:51.172 --> 34:54.884
I'm just like a mother duck to you.

34:54.967 --> 34:56.886
[Seung-hyo] Don't jump
to conclusions like that.

34:57.512 --> 34:59.055
It doesn't matter how you feel.

35:01.182 --> 35:03.017
It can't be helped if I'm not the one.

35:03.518 --> 35:04.685
But…

35:06.062 --> 35:07.688
don't tell me how I feel.

35:09.941 --> 35:11.818
No matter how much I like you,

35:13.945 --> 35:15.404
you have no right to do that.

35:17.073 --> 35:19.534
-Seung-hyo…
-The milk hasn't expired yet.

35:21.244 --> 35:23.121
And I'm not scared
of the jungle gym anymore.

35:40.429 --> 35:41.264
[music ends]

35:42.849 --> 35:44.267
[Jeong-u] Did you see the article?

35:45.017 --> 35:47.270
"They allow us to make it home

35:47.353 --> 35:50.815
to our friends and family
with a smile each day."

35:50.898 --> 35:54.694
"To our heroic paramedics
who protect our precious daily lives,

35:54.777 --> 35:56.571
I'd like to express my respect once more."

35:57.488 --> 35:59.574
-They even printed our picture.
-[Min-ho] Oh.

35:59.657 --> 36:01.742
I'm glad I used that sheet mask.

36:02.493 --> 36:04.120
Send me that link.

36:04.203 --> 36:06.122
I want to show my wife.

36:06.205 --> 36:07.290
[Jeong-u] Yes, sir.

36:09.625 --> 36:12.295
-Ms. Jung, isn't the article awesome?
-What?

36:13.087 --> 36:14.964
I don't know. I haven't read it yet.

36:15.047 --> 36:18.092
What? It's about us though.

36:18.176 --> 36:20.178
He put a lot of effort into it.
You should read it.

36:20.261 --> 36:22.597
I don't care about stuff like that.

36:23.097 --> 36:24.473
Just get back to work.

36:25.183 --> 36:26.142
[amusing music playing]

36:26.225 --> 36:28.144
[Jeong-u] Your picture
came out really well.

36:30.730 --> 36:32.106
PARAMEDICS ARE SO COOL

36:32.190 --> 36:33.566
THEY'RE AMAZING
I'M GRATEFUL

36:37.486 --> 36:38.321
MUDFLAT MAN

36:38.404 --> 36:39.530
[phone vibrating]

37:01.594 --> 37:05.056
I told you to just come in.
Why make it a hassle and call me out?

37:05.890 --> 37:09.477
Everyone's busy working,
so I didn't want to bother them.

37:09.560 --> 37:11.229
Do I not look busy?

37:11.312 --> 37:13.481
[chuckles] That's not what I meant.

37:13.564 --> 37:15.399
Please share this with the others.

37:15.483 --> 37:17.193
We're civil servants.
We can't accept this.

37:17.276 --> 37:20.154
I'm giving you this
as a fellow colleague, not a reporter,

37:20.238 --> 37:22.698
even if it was just for a day.

37:22.782 --> 37:23.908
Oh.

37:23.991 --> 37:27.161
You're really good
at making it hard to refuse things.

37:28.537 --> 37:30.289
Thank you. [chuckles softly]

37:30.873 --> 37:33.501
Thank you for helping me
write that article.

37:33.584 --> 37:35.962
I found my motivation again
thanks to you.

37:36.671 --> 37:39.298
Me? What did I do?

37:40.841 --> 37:41.842
Don't give anything up.

37:41.926 --> 37:43.886
My dad passed away when I was young.

37:44.387 --> 37:46.264
So I know what it's like.

37:46.347 --> 37:48.724
If my mom ever sacrificed
anything for me,

37:48.808 --> 37:51.060
I hated that the most.

37:51.143 --> 37:53.521
Someone got out of his car,

37:53.604 --> 37:55.982
and he directed traffic to clear the road.

37:56.565 --> 37:58.150
He was like a superhero.

37:58.234 --> 37:59.068
[chuckles softly]

37:59.819 --> 38:01.237
-You just did.
-[Mo-eum] What?

38:01.320 --> 38:03.239
I'll get going now.

38:04.115 --> 38:05.241
Bye.

38:07.159 --> 38:08.661
I LOVE YOU, MUDFLATS

38:08.744 --> 38:10.579
[heart thumping]

38:15.376 --> 38:16.335
[amusing music playing]

38:16.419 --> 38:18.129
-Dan-ho.
-Yes?

38:19.130 --> 38:21.966
From now on,
don't wear that T-shirt anymore.

38:22.049 --> 38:24.343
What? Why not?

38:24.427 --> 38:26.095
If I say not to wear it, just don't.

38:27.179 --> 38:28.055
[Mo-eum exclaims]

38:28.139 --> 38:29.807
Is that the only shirt you have?

38:29.890 --> 38:30.891
Is it your favorite?

38:31.684 --> 38:34.520
No, but it's really soft and stretchy.

38:34.603 --> 38:38.024
Yeah, sure. I'll buy you something nicer,
so don't wear it anymore.

38:38.107 --> 38:39.191
Oh.

38:39.275 --> 38:41.402
Why would you buy me clothes?

38:43.362 --> 38:44.780
You said we were colleagues.

38:45.448 --> 38:47.408
Colleagues can't buy each other shirts?

38:47.491 --> 38:49.118
No, it's not about that.

38:49.201 --> 38:50.119
[Mo-eum] Bye.

38:50.202 --> 38:51.829
-What?
-Go on.

38:54.707 --> 38:56.625
I need to get an ECG soon.

38:56.709 --> 38:59.003
Something's wrong. [sighs]

39:04.425 --> 39:05.343
But…

39:13.434 --> 39:14.268
[drill whirs]

39:15.186 --> 39:16.812
[mechanic] It's all fixed. [grunts]

39:16.896 --> 39:18.522
[Hye-suk] Thank you so much.

39:19.023 --> 39:20.941
But what caused it to break?

39:21.025 --> 39:22.318
Well…

39:23.986 --> 39:25.696
I found this inside the washer.

39:26.364 --> 39:27.573
[Hye-suk] Goodness.

39:28.616 --> 39:29.492
Wait.

39:30.951 --> 39:32.328
Why would this be in…

39:32.870 --> 39:35.206
[mechanic] I think
the spoon caused the issue.

39:35.289 --> 39:36.916
It could've been really bad.

39:38.626 --> 39:40.753
Thank you. Have a nice day.

39:40.836 --> 39:43.672
-All right. Have a good day.
-[Hye-suk] Thank you very much.

39:43.756 --> 39:45.383
-Thank you for your work.
-No problem.

39:45.466 --> 39:47.760
-[Hye-suk] Have a nice day.
-[mechanic] You too.

39:48.719 --> 39:51.472
-[Seung-hyo] Did something break?
-[Hye-suk] No, it was nothing.

39:51.555 --> 39:53.641
[chuckles nervously] Hey, Seung-hyo.

39:54.850 --> 39:57.311
-[door closes]
-Have you had trouble sleeping lately?

39:57.395 --> 39:59.063
No. Why?

39:59.146 --> 40:01.607
You look pale,
and your light stays on at night.

40:02.483 --> 40:03.317
Oh.

40:03.401 --> 40:05.027
I've been busy with work.

40:05.111 --> 40:07.363
-[phone vibrating]
-I see. Poor thing.

40:07.446 --> 40:09.281
Go ahead. Take it.

40:11.283 --> 40:12.284
Hello?

40:13.077 --> 40:14.370
Hey, Myeong-u.

40:16.664 --> 40:17.748
What?

40:17.832 --> 40:19.208
[tense music playing]

40:20.876 --> 40:22.211
-Myeong-u!
-Hey, Mr. Choi.

40:22.294 --> 40:25.089
They told us to stop construction?
What's going on?

40:25.589 --> 40:27.842
The district office got a complaint
and said to stop now.

40:27.925 --> 40:28.759
[Seung-hyo] Wait.

40:28.843 --> 40:32.054
We got consent from everyone in the area.
Why would this happen?

40:32.138 --> 40:33.597
Someone next door complained.

40:33.681 --> 40:35.724
Right to light
and obstruction of view or whatever.

40:35.808 --> 40:37.893
That's ridiculous.
I checked several times.

40:37.977 --> 40:38.811
[Myeong-u] I know.

40:38.894 --> 40:39.937
I discussed things already

40:40.020 --> 40:42.022
with the official in charge
to not violate rules.

40:42.106 --> 40:44.942
You did, but they said
the person in charge changed.

40:45.025 --> 40:45.860
[sighs]

40:48.154 --> 40:50.698
That means we have to
start everything over again.

40:51.949 --> 40:54.326
Let's meet with the people
who filed the complaint first.

40:54.410 --> 40:56.620
Persuading them will be the priority.

40:56.704 --> 40:57.830
[man] Well, look at this!

40:58.414 --> 41:01.584
Are the people trying to build
this great building finally here?

41:01.667 --> 41:03.502
[whispering] Speak of the devil. It's him.

41:05.129 --> 41:06.380
[in normal voice] Hello, sir.

41:06.464 --> 41:09.467
I'm the CEO of the architectural firm
that designed this building.

41:09.550 --> 41:14.221
May I ask about the kind of inconvenience
you had during construction?

41:14.305 --> 41:16.599
There were so many, I can't name them all!

41:16.682 --> 41:19.018
There's no need to discuss it.
Get rid of this now.

41:19.101 --> 41:22.396
Sir, you agreed
to the construction last time.

41:22.480 --> 41:24.482
I allowed you
to build a house on the land,

41:24.565 --> 41:26.108
not to extend it into the sky!

41:26.192 --> 41:27.943
They say you need
more sunlight as you age,

41:28.027 --> 41:30.154
but this house will shorten my lifespan!

41:30.237 --> 41:31.864
I only get a tiny bit of sun.

41:31.947 --> 41:33.782
Half the sky's covered now.

41:33.866 --> 41:35.159
You think that's all?

41:35.242 --> 41:37.536
The ground has sloped.

41:37.620 --> 41:39.455
And the flowers have wilted
from the noise.

41:39.538 --> 41:41.832
Sure, fine. I can understand all that.

41:41.916 --> 41:44.418
But we made the groundwater suddenly flow?

41:44.502 --> 41:47.046
That's too much, isn't it?

41:47.755 --> 41:50.257
[Na-yun] Still, to show us,

41:50.341 --> 41:52.551
wasn't it funny when he came
with a bent wire hanger?

41:52.635 --> 41:53.761
[all laughing]

41:55.763 --> 41:56.931
Hey, it really was.

41:57.014 --> 41:58.849
-It started to move!
-Yeah!

42:01.477 --> 42:03.354
You two can both leave.

42:03.437 --> 42:05.189
-Sorry.
-I'm sorry.

42:05.981 --> 42:08.067
I think this was his plan from the start.

42:08.150 --> 42:10.611
He asked a lot of questions
whenever we came on-site.

42:10.694 --> 42:12.530
He looked at things very closely.

42:12.613 --> 42:14.615
[sighs] What he really wants
is a settlement.

42:14.698 --> 42:17.535
He agreed at first,
but now, he's having second thoughts.

42:18.118 --> 42:19.870
Then, what do we do now?

42:21.580 --> 42:25.501
But didn't we already obtain
the project cooperation agreement?

42:25.584 --> 42:26.418
[gasps]

42:26.502 --> 42:29.088
Yeah, we did
to prepare for something like this.

42:29.588 --> 42:33.008
Even if there's a worst-case scenario
of a civil lawsuit, it can be dismissed.

42:33.092 --> 42:35.344
Goodness! Why didn't I think of that?

42:35.427 --> 42:36.845
Right? Hey, who obtained it?

42:36.929 --> 42:38.806
-I did.
-[Myeong-u] Go and get it.

42:38.889 --> 42:42.017
Let's take this chance to show them
the importance of a signed document.

42:42.518 --> 42:44.019
-Stop smiling and go get it!
-Oh, me.

42:44.520 --> 42:46.272
-I'll be right back.
-[Myeong-u] Okay.

42:46.355 --> 42:48.232
[sighs] That should do it.

42:48.315 --> 42:50.776
THE NOT-SO-SIMPLE CURIOSITY OF KANG DAN-HO
HEROES OF OUR TIME

42:50.859 --> 42:51.902
[pleasant music playing]

42:53.737 --> 42:54.780
[telephone ringing]

42:59.535 --> 43:00.452
[chuckles softly]

43:04.498 --> 43:05.624
[music distorts]

43:05.708 --> 43:08.168
Just climb inside your monitor,
why don't you?

43:08.252 --> 43:11.088
[Dan-ho exclaims] Why do you keep
popping up behind me?

43:11.171 --> 43:12.381
It's going to cause problems.

43:12.464 --> 43:15.676
-I'll report it as workplace harassment.
-I'll report you too.

43:15.759 --> 43:18.887
I'll say a journalist is writing
with personal bias, not objectivity.

43:20.681 --> 43:21.890
When did I ever do that?

43:21.974 --> 43:24.602
You suddenly wanted
to write about your experiences…

43:25.519 --> 43:26.353
because of her?

43:27.104 --> 43:28.480
The paramedic you know?

43:28.564 --> 43:30.649
-Well…
-[Yeong-in] I knew it.

43:30.733 --> 43:33.360
I could sense the affection in your words.

43:33.444 --> 43:34.653
And I was right. [claps hands]

43:34.737 --> 43:36.947
It was due to your love for the subject.

43:37.031 --> 43:38.407
It's not like that.

43:38.490 --> 43:40.743
If there's any personal bias
in this article,

43:40.826 --> 43:42.661
it's out of respect and reverence.

43:42.745 --> 43:45.164
-Okay? Yeah.
-[Yeong-in] Yeah? Okay.

43:45.247 --> 43:47.124
Is that so? I see.

43:47.207 --> 43:48.500
[amusing music playing]

43:49.460 --> 43:51.503
Gosh, but she really is pretty.

43:53.088 --> 43:54.173
Good luck!

43:56.634 --> 43:59.011
Complimenting someone's looks
is a form of judgment too.

44:00.679 --> 44:02.139
[whispering] And don't wish me luck!

44:04.600 --> 44:06.268
[man in normal voice] Good luck, Dan-ho.

44:06.769 --> 44:09.688
Hey! Don't eavesdrop.

44:09.772 --> 44:11.357
[man] It's because I can hear you.

44:12.149 --> 44:14.610
-Stop.
-[man] What does she look like?

44:14.693 --> 44:15.611
God.

44:15.694 --> 44:17.946
[Mo-eum] "I could sense the true essence

44:18.030 --> 44:20.616
of heroism from the spirit
of these paramedics."

44:21.617 --> 44:22.868
"And I thought about it."

44:23.661 --> 44:26.580
"If the Avengers had paramedics,

44:28.040 --> 44:33.128
wouldn't they have defeated
Thanos more easily?"

44:33.629 --> 44:34.463
Wow.

44:35.089 --> 44:36.507
Nice article.

44:36.590 --> 44:37.424
[Mo-eum] Hey.

44:38.300 --> 44:40.219
It's not just nice.

44:40.803 --> 44:44.848
This is a masterpiece
that will go down in history.

44:45.557 --> 44:49.561
You can feel the authenticity of someone
who experienced things firsthand.

44:50.771 --> 44:51.772
[chuckles softly]

44:52.272 --> 44:55.526
Goodness, he worked so hard that day too.

44:56.443 --> 44:59.113
With these little hands that have
probably only touched keyboards,

44:59.196 --> 45:02.783
he wanted to do all he could to help out.

45:04.451 --> 45:07.037
Goodness.
I think that's how he normally is.

45:07.663 --> 45:09.832
He leads by example, and he's just.

45:11.458 --> 45:15.921
Well, that's probably why
he was Mudflat Man.

45:17.005 --> 45:19.258
You've fallen head over heels
for Mudflat Man.

45:19.341 --> 45:22.761
You're knee-high in mud.
You won't be able to free yourself easily.

45:22.845 --> 45:23.720
What?

45:23.804 --> 45:26.890
Did you know you've been talking
about him for 30 minutes now?

45:26.974 --> 45:28.475
Hey, that's because…

45:29.143 --> 45:31.270
[laughing] Hey, you!

45:32.062 --> 45:35.232
That was because it's a good article.

45:35.315 --> 45:38.026
[laughingly] It was praise
for his professionalism.

45:38.110 --> 45:39.361
[amusing music playing]

45:40.237 --> 45:41.363
Gosh, that's so funny.

45:45.159 --> 45:50.664
People usually look cool
when they excel at their job.

45:52.416 --> 45:55.669
Even Seung-hyo looks all right
when he's designing.

45:55.752 --> 45:57.713
What are you talking about?

45:57.796 --> 46:00.799
Seung-hyo? Don't be ridiculous.

46:00.883 --> 46:01.884
Hey.

46:02.426 --> 46:04.219
Has he said anything recently?

46:04.303 --> 46:07.347
I don't know.
I haven't seen him in a while.

46:07.931 --> 46:09.141
Really?

46:13.937 --> 46:15.355
Yes, that's right.

46:16.440 --> 46:17.441
Yes.

46:19.735 --> 46:21.904
-Yes, I understand.
-[line disconnects]

46:21.987 --> 46:24.198
-What did the official say?
-It's as expected.

46:25.032 --> 46:28.327
They have no choice but to stop things
when they get a complaint.

46:28.827 --> 46:30.579
They said we should reach a settlement.

46:31.955 --> 46:33.165
Should I meet with him again?

46:33.248 --> 46:35.834
If it's not possible, we'll just settle it
at a reasonable price.

46:35.918 --> 46:36.752
No.

46:37.252 --> 46:40.881
More people will try to exploit us
if we give in to unreasonable demands.

46:41.757 --> 46:43.717
We can't create a bad precedent.

46:44.301 --> 46:45.594
-[knock on door]
-[sighs softly]

46:46.261 --> 46:47.304
Come in.

46:50.057 --> 46:51.225
[Seung-hyo] Hey.

46:51.308 --> 46:53.560
-Did you bring the agreement?
-[door closes]

46:54.144 --> 46:55.437
Well… [exhales]

46:58.232 --> 46:59.399
I'm sorry, Mr. Choi.

47:00.400 --> 47:01.735
The agreement…

47:02.569 --> 47:03.403
I lost it.

47:04.154 --> 47:05.614
-What?
-[Myeong-u] What?

47:05.697 --> 47:08.158
[stuttering] Where did it go?

47:08.242 --> 47:10.494
I have no idea.

47:10.577 --> 47:12.746
I got it that day
and put it somewhere safe.

47:12.829 --> 47:15.249
I checked the bookshelf,
my desk, and the trunk of my car.

47:15.332 --> 47:17.668
I spent hours looking for it,
but I can't find it.

47:17.751 --> 47:21.213
Are you kidding me?
Is this the best you can do?

47:21.880 --> 47:23.549
-I'm sorry.
-Sorry is not enough!

47:23.632 --> 47:25.676
You think an apology will fix this?

47:25.759 --> 47:26.969
-Myeong-u, wait.
-I mean…

47:27.052 --> 47:28.303
Don't get worked up. Calm down.

47:28.387 --> 47:30.138
-Hyeong-chan.
-Yes?

47:30.222 --> 47:33.100
Do you understand
the gravity of your mistake?

47:33.183 --> 47:35.686
I've caused significant damage
to the company.

47:35.769 --> 47:37.020
You're not wrong.

47:37.563 --> 47:39.982
Delaying construction
will push the schedule back

47:40.065 --> 47:41.692
and increase costs.

47:42.442 --> 47:44.486
But do you know
what's more important than that?

47:45.737 --> 47:47.072
I don't know, sir.

47:47.155 --> 47:48.865
Go and think about it.

47:49.992 --> 47:52.869
And come back when you find that answer.

47:52.953 --> 47:53.954
Yes, sir.

47:55.831 --> 47:56.832
I'm sorry.

48:00.711 --> 48:01.712
[door closes]

48:01.795 --> 48:04.506
But what's the answer?
I don't know what it is either.

48:05.591 --> 48:07.259
[sighs] This is driving me crazy.

48:11.888 --> 48:13.599
[Mi-suk] Did you drop money on the ground?

48:15.684 --> 48:18.478
-Why do you have your head down?
-Hi, Aunt Mi-suk.

48:18.979 --> 48:20.147
Have you had dinner?

48:21.815 --> 48:22.774
[exhales]

48:26.194 --> 48:29.531
Why would you feed me?
Aren't you mad at me for deceiving you?

48:30.407 --> 48:32.075
I don't understand myself either.

48:32.743 --> 48:35.621
But what can I do?
I can tell something's up with you.

48:38.540 --> 48:39.499
How did you know?

48:39.583 --> 48:41.877
I raised you myself.

48:41.960 --> 48:43.420
You're like my child.

48:46.423 --> 48:47.299
Aunt Mi-suk,

48:47.966 --> 48:50.469
I'm sorry
I didn't tell you about Seok-ryu.

48:51.053 --> 48:52.721
That wasn't your fault.

48:53.680 --> 48:55.557
I shouldn't have taken it out on you.

48:57.267 --> 48:58.101
But the thing is…

48:59.770 --> 49:02.022
Seok-ryu's really serious about it.

49:02.105 --> 49:04.941
You cut me some slack.
Can't you do the same for her?

49:07.653 --> 49:08.570
Eat up.

49:09.154 --> 49:11.782
You're abandoning me
because you don't want to hear it?

49:11.865 --> 49:14.826
There's a neighborhood meeting.
I'll get fined if I miss it.

49:14.910 --> 49:15.744
A fine?

49:17.037 --> 49:17.913
How much is it?

49:19.081 --> 49:22.709
How much will it cost
to sit at a table with you?

49:22.793 --> 49:25.796
You little… How dare you flaunt your money
by impersonating Han Suk-kyu?

49:27.839 --> 49:29.716
-Eat as much as you want.
-[Seung-hyo] Okay.

49:31.385 --> 49:32.386
[clicks tongue]

49:38.809 --> 49:39.768
[door opens]

49:40.769 --> 49:41.770
[door closes]

49:43.647 --> 49:44.481
[door opens]

49:44.564 --> 49:46.233
[footsteps approaching]

49:55.325 --> 49:58.704
-I didn't know you were home.
-I didn't know you were here either.

49:59.871 --> 50:00.706
Where's my mom?

50:01.206 --> 50:03.375
-She went to a neighborhood meeting.
-I see.

50:05.335 --> 50:06.420
Eat up.

50:07.337 --> 50:08.380
Why are you avoiding me?

50:09.047 --> 50:09.881
I'm not.

50:09.965 --> 50:13.218
I came to the kitchen
to drink something, but I forgot.

50:15.095 --> 50:17.222
DAEHAN MILK

50:19.891 --> 50:20.726
Hey, Choisseung.

50:22.519 --> 50:23.437
What?

50:25.188 --> 50:26.440
Throw out that milk.

50:28.608 --> 50:29.568
What?

50:30.569 --> 50:32.070
I'm answering you in advance.

50:33.238 --> 50:34.114
To me,

50:34.656 --> 50:36.283
you can't be more than a friend.

50:39.745 --> 50:40.871
Is that all you have to say?

50:41.913 --> 50:43.206
Yeah, I'm sorry.

50:45.333 --> 50:47.419
There's no room for reconsideration?

50:50.380 --> 50:51.465
No.

50:52.215 --> 50:53.341
[emotional music playing]

50:53.425 --> 50:56.636
It'll be awkward for a few days,
but it'll get better soon.

50:57.888 --> 51:02.225
Our friendship wouldn't break that easily
over something like this.

51:05.979 --> 51:10.942
Eat and put the dishes
in the sink before you leave.

51:14.112 --> 51:15.197
Friendship?

51:16.615 --> 51:18.200
There's no such thing as that anymore.

51:18.742 --> 51:20.285
[slow pop song playing]

51:27.292 --> 51:28.418
[exhales]

51:55.946 --> 51:57.113
Hyeon-jun,

51:57.948 --> 51:59.658
do you remember when I first got sick?

52:01.701 --> 52:03.578
They removed two-thirds of my stomach

52:04.329 --> 52:07.082
and I lost ten kilograms
after starting chemotherapy.

52:10.418 --> 52:11.378
Chemotherapy…

52:12.921 --> 52:13.964
I hear it's hard.

52:14.548 --> 52:15.674
It's okay.

52:16.299 --> 52:18.218
I dealt with surgery pretty easily.

52:19.594 --> 52:22.430
I'm Bae Seok-ryu. I'll overcome this.

52:23.223 --> 52:24.516
Don't worry.

52:31.815 --> 52:33.275
Once I recover,

52:34.192 --> 52:36.111
should we go to Salar de Uyuni?

52:36.194 --> 52:37.696
-Uyuni?
-Yeah.

52:37.779 --> 52:39.865
No, wait.

52:42.492 --> 52:45.954
Should we go to Peru
to visit Machu Picchu?

52:46.538 --> 52:47.747
Machu Picchu.

52:47.831 --> 52:49.499
-Peru.
-Where do you want to go?

52:50.166 --> 52:52.085
-We can visit both.
-Both?

52:53.461 --> 52:54.504
Sounds good.

53:03.096 --> 53:05.515
-I applied to return to work.
-Already?

53:06.474 --> 53:09.561
I'm all better now,
so I should go back to work.

53:10.395 --> 53:11.730
Aren't you overdoing it?

53:12.397 --> 53:14.941
I can't stay like this forever.

53:15.692 --> 53:17.110
So what if I was sick?

53:17.193 --> 53:18.862
I can overcome anything with my will.

53:21.656 --> 53:22.657
[chuckles softly]

53:22.741 --> 53:25.452
[Hyeon-jun] Seok-ryu, you're incredible.

53:25.535 --> 53:27.746
It's what I thought as I watched you.

53:28.330 --> 53:31.207
You're so much stronger
and more resilient than I thought.

53:32.584 --> 53:33.585
I really respect you.

53:34.836 --> 53:35.962
And I love you.

53:39.341 --> 53:40.759
[song continues playing]

54:05.450 --> 54:06.451
Seok-ryu.

54:07.285 --> 54:10.956
Raymond invited us
to his vacation home in Palm Springs.

54:11.039 --> 54:12.082
He said to come with you.

54:12.749 --> 54:14.501
[weakly] I just want to stay at home.

54:14.584 --> 54:16.044
Don't be like that. Let's go.

54:16.544 --> 54:18.254
We haven't gone anywhere for a while.

54:18.964 --> 54:21.132
It's always been
the hospital, home, and work.

54:21.216 --> 54:23.009
[weakly] No, I don't want to.

54:23.677 --> 54:28.556
The doctor said plenty of sunlight
would help with the depression.

54:30.517 --> 54:33.228
Have you been actively attending
your therapy sessions?

54:34.020 --> 54:35.105
Are you taking your meds?

54:35.855 --> 54:36.856
Yeah.

54:38.525 --> 54:39.484
Okay.

54:40.986 --> 54:42.445
That way, you'll get better.

54:44.114 --> 54:46.241
I'll tell Raymond we can't go.

54:47.117 --> 54:48.702
I'll say we're busy with the wedding.

54:48.785 --> 54:50.203
[solemn music playing]

54:50.954 --> 54:52.872
By the way, did you hear?

54:52.956 --> 54:56.126
Well, it's about why she took
a break from work three years ago.

54:56.209 --> 54:59.587
That? That was quite big,
what happened to her.

55:03.258 --> 55:05.260
[whispering] She has stomach cancer.

55:05.885 --> 55:06.720
[Susan] Really?

55:06.803 --> 55:08.638
-[Chris] Yeah, to think…
-[Susan sighs]

55:08.722 --> 55:12.350
…she returned to the office
after literally working herself to death,

55:12.851 --> 55:16.354
I don't know
whether to call it crazy or…

55:16.438 --> 55:18.440
-Oh, crazy.
-[Susan chuckles]

55:18.523 --> 55:19.983
[Peter] Talk about a loyal dog.

55:20.066 --> 55:21.026
[Chris] Exactly.

55:21.109 --> 55:24.070
That girl really doesn't know
how to take care of herself, huh?

55:24.154 --> 55:25.363
[exhales]

55:26.114 --> 55:27.532
Poor little girl.

55:27.615 --> 55:29.159
[music continues playing]

55:32.412 --> 55:33.747
[people laughing]

55:38.626 --> 55:41.629
[Seok-ryu breathing heavily]

55:54.726 --> 55:56.019
What do you think you're doing?

55:57.812 --> 55:59.272
[Hyeon-jun] Seok-ryu?

56:02.358 --> 56:04.527
[breathes deeply]

56:06.696 --> 56:08.156
[breathes deeply]

56:14.621 --> 56:16.247
How could you not trust me?

56:16.831 --> 56:18.750
Why didn't you pick up your phone then?

56:20.543 --> 56:22.545
You're the one who ghosted me first.

56:22.629 --> 56:23.963
Still…

56:25.423 --> 56:27.509
Did you really have to show up like that?

56:27.592 --> 56:28.718
What?

56:29.719 --> 56:31.054
Are you embarrassed of me?

56:32.305 --> 56:34.724
-Are you ashamed?
-[Hyeon-jun] No, it's not that.

56:36.559 --> 56:38.561
Everyone I work with was there.

56:40.188 --> 56:43.525
As my fiancée,
you should've considered my perspective.

56:43.608 --> 56:45.276
Am I really your fiancée though?

56:46.528 --> 56:48.947
-What?
-Your fiancée is sick.

56:49.989 --> 56:53.243
She's going through a hard time.
But you wanted to go to a party?

56:55.203 --> 56:57.622
You don't care about how I feel.

56:58.248 --> 57:01.000
Did you want to have fun
with others at that party?

57:01.084 --> 57:02.168
Yeah.

57:03.044 --> 57:04.254
I did.

57:06.172 --> 57:07.173
Please let me breathe!

57:11.970 --> 57:13.596
When you became sick,

57:14.097 --> 57:15.473
I gave up everything.

57:16.141 --> 57:18.143
I took time off work
and cared for you.

57:18.226 --> 57:20.645
I put golf, traveling,
my friends, and my life on hold.

57:20.728 --> 57:23.189
I thought things would be fine
if I endured a little more.

57:23.982 --> 57:26.860
Because you're strong.
Because you're going to beat this!

57:26.943 --> 57:27.777
We…

57:29.737 --> 57:31.614
Because we'll overcome it together.

57:31.698 --> 57:33.074
But suddenly, what?

57:34.200 --> 57:36.286
[sighs wearily] This goddamn depression…

57:42.208 --> 57:44.002
"This goddamn depression"?

57:45.712 --> 57:47.297
Is that what you were thinking?

57:49.799 --> 57:50.884
You said you understood me.

57:51.634 --> 57:52.677
How can I?

57:54.429 --> 57:55.847
How can I understand you?

57:56.723 --> 57:59.767
You finished your treatment,
but now, you're not yourself.

57:59.851 --> 58:02.979
You're not the Seok-ryu I know.
How can I accept that?

58:03.521 --> 58:05.023
Please snap out of it.

58:05.690 --> 58:08.067
How long are you going to struggle
with that depression for?

58:08.735 --> 58:11.029
If you drag me down
with you to the bottom,

58:11.112 --> 58:12.530
are you going to stop then?

58:16.075 --> 58:17.327
[music fades]

58:22.582 --> 58:23.625
[sighs]

58:23.708 --> 58:25.126
Seok-ryu.

58:25.210 --> 58:27.337
Look, what I just said…

58:27.420 --> 58:29.005
I'm already at rock bottom.

58:30.590 --> 58:31.966
Hyeon-jun.

58:34.260 --> 58:36.471
I just witnessed our rock bottom.

58:49.484 --> 58:50.944
[slow music playing]

58:51.027 --> 58:52.529
The ring's too big.

58:53.029 --> 58:57.158
-It fit perfectly back then.
-It's because you've lost weight.

58:57.659 --> 59:01.246
It's okay. Let's go back
to the US and get it resized.

59:03.164 --> 59:05.250
[Seok-ryu] We can fix the ring,

59:07.919 --> 59:09.754
but we can't fix our relationship.

59:10.880 --> 59:12.382
Seok-ryu.

59:14.050 --> 59:15.301
I'm really sorry

59:16.261 --> 59:17.720
for what happened back then.

59:18.680 --> 59:20.139
It was so hard for me.

59:21.266 --> 59:24.644
-I was tired and out of my mind.
-You don't have to apologize to me.

59:26.104 --> 59:28.731
You really tried your best.

59:29.524 --> 59:30.817
I know that better than anyone.

59:32.735 --> 59:35.780
It's just too much for me.

59:38.491 --> 59:39.617
You know,

59:40.118 --> 59:43.288
I'm going to worry
about a recurrence next year

59:43.913 --> 59:45.498
and the year after that.

59:47.584 --> 59:50.253
Even if I remain
in complete remission for five years,

59:52.255 --> 59:54.215
I won't be completely free.

59:56.801 --> 59:59.512
I'll always be near death's door.

01:00:01.389 --> 01:00:04.350
I'm going to feel
a little anxious and sad.

01:00:08.605 --> 01:00:10.523
That's how my life's going to be.

01:00:12.942 --> 01:00:13.985
That's why…

01:00:14.986 --> 01:00:16.446
I don't need love anymore.

01:00:18.281 --> 01:00:19.699
The stomach I have left

01:00:20.825 --> 01:00:23.036
can barely handle digesting my dream.

01:00:34.756 --> 01:00:37.008
[sighs deeply]

01:00:51.773 --> 01:00:54.776
[doctor] The endoscopy showed
some inflammation where the surgery was.

01:00:54.859 --> 01:00:56.986
It's highly likely
to be just inflammation,

01:00:57.070 --> 01:00:59.572
but we've conducted a biopsy to be sure.

01:00:59.656 --> 01:01:01.282
The results will be out in a few days.

01:01:03.910 --> 01:01:04.827
Good job.

01:01:06.746 --> 01:01:08.122
It was the right thing to do.

01:01:09.749 --> 01:01:10.792
This is right.

01:01:33.564 --> 01:01:35.274
[slow music fades]

01:01:43.741 --> 01:01:44.784
What is it?

01:01:44.867 --> 01:01:46.661
Is my food not good?

01:01:47.245 --> 01:01:48.079
It's not that.

01:01:49.747 --> 01:01:51.457
I have no appetite.

01:01:52.917 --> 01:01:54.836
Still, you should eat.

01:01:55.461 --> 01:01:58.798
Balanced growth and development
are a child's responsibility.

01:01:58.881 --> 01:01:59.924
[Yeon-du scoffs]

01:02:00.007 --> 01:02:02.051
Children have too many responsibilities.

01:02:03.636 --> 01:02:05.388
I have to eat this carrot.

01:02:05.888 --> 01:02:07.765
I have to brush my teeth.

01:02:07.849 --> 01:02:09.183
And I have to sleep early.

01:02:09.267 --> 01:02:10.184
[chuckles softly]

01:02:10.768 --> 01:02:12.103
[phone vibrating]

01:02:13.479 --> 01:02:14.772
YEON-DU'S BABYSITTER

01:02:15.732 --> 01:02:16.607
Hello?

01:02:18.860 --> 01:02:20.778
Oh, are you okay?

01:02:22.196 --> 01:02:24.282
Of course, your health is most important.

01:02:25.116 --> 01:02:27.952
You should go to the hospital.
Let me know when you know the results.

01:02:29.704 --> 01:02:30.788
Okay.

01:02:31.914 --> 01:02:33.708
-[line disconnects]
-What was that about?

01:02:33.791 --> 01:02:37.503
Your babysitter fell in the bathroom
and hurt her back.

01:02:38.671 --> 01:02:41.007
I guess you're hanging out with me today.

01:02:41.090 --> 01:02:43.843
You said you had
an important interview today.

01:02:43.926 --> 01:02:46.763
There's nothing
more important to me than you.

01:02:49.724 --> 01:02:51.058
No, you should go.

01:02:51.142 --> 01:02:53.144
I have a friend I can play with.

01:02:54.562 --> 01:02:55.396
Who?

01:02:55.480 --> 01:02:56.939
[quirky music playing]

01:02:57.023 --> 01:02:58.483
You want to hang out with me?

01:02:58.566 --> 01:02:59.484
-Yes.
-[Mo-eum gasps]

01:03:00.401 --> 01:03:03.780
I'd love that! I'm so happy! But…

01:03:03.863 --> 01:03:05.072
What do I do?

01:03:05.156 --> 01:03:07.283
I have something important to do today.

01:03:07.366 --> 01:03:09.035
I was on my way out.

01:03:09.619 --> 01:03:10.870
[Dan-ho] I'm sorry.

01:03:10.953 --> 01:03:12.914
It was an unreasonable request, wasn't it?

01:03:14.957 --> 01:03:18.503
Yeon-du, let's hang out
with Ms. Jung next time.

01:03:19.462 --> 01:03:20.338
Wait!

01:03:21.339 --> 01:03:23.466
I have a good idea.

01:03:26.594 --> 01:03:28.304
[exclaims]

01:03:29.972 --> 01:03:33.309
[Jae-suk] Mo-eum called to let me know.
Don't worry. Leave her with us.

01:03:33.392 --> 01:03:34.602
-Hi, Yeon-du.
-Thank you.

01:03:34.685 --> 01:03:36.103
Sit between them.

01:03:36.187 --> 01:03:37.688
[In-suk] You're so cute.

01:03:37.772 --> 01:03:40.191
I couldn't come empty-handed.
Please accept this.

01:03:40.274 --> 01:03:42.819
[Jae-suk] Goodness.
You didn't have to buy this.

01:03:42.902 --> 01:03:44.070
But what is it?

01:03:44.153 --> 01:03:47.657
It's a health supplement.
It helps with managing your blood sugar.

01:03:47.740 --> 01:03:49.325
Goodness.

01:03:49.408 --> 01:03:53.120
My blood sugar does spike after a meal.
This is the perfect gift.

01:03:53.788 --> 01:03:54.747
Thank you so much.

01:03:55.540 --> 01:03:57.834
Can we all try it?

01:03:57.917 --> 01:03:59.377
-[Jae-suk laughing]
-Yes, of course.

01:03:59.460 --> 01:04:00.294
Thank you.

01:04:01.045 --> 01:04:02.672
I know it's shameless of me,

01:04:02.755 --> 01:04:05.383
but please take good care of Yeon-du.

01:04:05.466 --> 01:04:06.759
[Jae-suk] Don't worry.

01:04:06.843 --> 01:04:08.261
Yeon-du, I'll be back later.

01:04:08.344 --> 01:04:09.720
Have a good day.

01:04:10.304 --> 01:04:12.890
Drive carefully and don't trip again.

01:04:12.974 --> 01:04:14.684
-Okay.
-[Jae-suk] Goodness.

01:04:14.767 --> 01:04:16.394
Have a great day.

01:04:17.520 --> 01:04:18.563
-The scissors.
-Okay.

01:04:18.646 --> 01:04:20.189
Can I drink two?

01:04:20.273 --> 01:04:21.482
Just drink one.

01:04:22.108 --> 01:04:23.860
-Jae-suk, who was that?
-Our neighbor.

01:04:23.985 --> 01:04:26.028
-[Hye-suk] Your client?
-[Jae-suk] He was.

01:04:26.112 --> 01:04:26.946
HODANGWON

01:04:29.490 --> 01:04:31.492
-Do you want one?
-No, I'm fine.

01:04:31.576 --> 01:04:32.451
[In-suk] Why not?

01:04:32.952 --> 01:04:34.912
-[Hye-suk] What's your name?
-[exclaims]

01:04:34.996 --> 01:04:36.330
Kang Yeon-du.

01:04:36.414 --> 01:04:38.875
I was born in the spring.

01:04:38.958 --> 01:04:41.669
My name means "to live with vitality,"

01:04:41.752 --> 01:04:45.131
like the vibrant color of the first leaves
that emerge after winter.

01:04:45.214 --> 01:04:47.550
What a great name.

01:04:47.633 --> 01:04:49.468
You're smart and clever, aren't you?

01:04:49.552 --> 01:04:51.804
Her dad's a journalist,
so she's smart too.

01:04:51.888 --> 01:04:54.432
So that's why you said he was off-limits.

01:04:54.515 --> 01:04:55.766
[Jae-suk] Yeah.

01:04:55.850 --> 01:04:56.767
Yeon-du.

01:04:56.851 --> 01:04:59.020
Let's have a blast today.

01:04:59.103 --> 01:05:01.606
We can't be the only ones
enjoying something.

01:05:01.689 --> 01:05:02.565
Right?

01:05:02.648 --> 01:05:03.900
Here.

01:05:03.983 --> 01:05:05.484
Auntie got this as a free gift.

01:05:05.568 --> 01:05:07.612
You're more like a granny than an auntie.

01:05:07.695 --> 01:05:08.863
-What?
-[Mi-suk] Goodness.

01:05:08.946 --> 01:05:09.780
Granny?

01:05:09.864 --> 01:05:11.157
[Mi-suk laughing]

01:05:11.240 --> 01:05:15.536
Hey, people still think
I'm in my early forties.

01:05:16.370 --> 01:05:17.371
I don't know.

01:05:17.455 --> 01:05:19.749
They say the eyes of children
are the most honest.

01:05:19.832 --> 01:05:22.501
I bet she could become a reporter
like her dad.

01:05:22.585 --> 01:05:24.003
She's brutally honest.

01:05:24.086 --> 01:05:26.964
-[all chuckling]
-I should increase my collagen intake.

01:05:27.048 --> 01:05:29.717
Anyway, you can have this.

01:05:29.800 --> 01:05:32.929
-Thank you.
-[laughing]

01:05:33.012 --> 01:05:35.890
-Can kids eat red ginseng?
-[In-suk] Of course.

01:05:35.973 --> 01:05:38.059
It has good ingredients.

01:05:38.142 --> 01:05:40.311
What was it called again?

01:05:40.394 --> 01:05:41.520
[amusing music playing]

01:05:41.604 --> 01:05:42.730
Saffron.

01:05:42.813 --> 01:05:45.900
You consume so much medicine,
and you still don't know that?

01:05:45.983 --> 01:05:46.943
What?

01:05:47.026 --> 01:05:50.655
It's not saffron.
Are you sure it's not saponin?

01:05:50.738 --> 01:05:52.156
[In-suk] Yeah, it is.

01:05:52.239 --> 01:05:54.116
I thought it was saponin too.

01:05:54.200 --> 01:05:55.785
-Saponin…
-[Hye-suk] I…

01:05:55.868 --> 01:05:57.578
That's what I said too.

01:05:57.662 --> 01:05:59.372
-Yeah, right.
-[all laughing]

01:05:59.455 --> 01:06:01.374
You said it was saffron.

01:06:02.333 --> 01:06:03.793
No, my pronunciation was bad.

01:06:03.876 --> 01:06:05.711
-[all laughing]
-Hey.

01:06:06.295 --> 01:06:07.546
-Hey.
-Are you joking?

01:06:07.630 --> 01:06:09.840
I can see how you could've misheard me.

01:06:09.924 --> 01:06:10.925
No way.

01:06:11.759 --> 01:06:16.013
The great Seo Hye-suk
falls from her throne.

01:06:16.097 --> 01:06:18.808
It's saffron.
That sounds like the name of a detergent.

01:06:18.891 --> 01:06:21.102
I know it's saponin too.

01:06:21.185 --> 01:06:22.520
Saponin!

01:06:22.603 --> 01:06:24.605
-Saponin!
-[Jae-suk] Right?

01:06:24.689 --> 01:06:26.107
[all laughing]

01:06:27.692 --> 01:06:30.778
Saffron is a spice. It's very expensive.

01:06:30.861 --> 01:06:32.905
[everyone chattering]

01:06:35.825 --> 01:06:37.118
-[camera clicks]
-[exhales]

01:06:37.201 --> 01:06:38.619
[mischievous music playing]

01:06:41.038 --> 01:06:42.206
[camera clicks]

01:06:45.918 --> 01:06:48.629
[exhales] What should I write
to reel people in?

01:06:52.633 --> 01:06:56.804
Do you want the muscles of a bodybuilder?

01:06:57.722 --> 01:07:03.936
"I selected this product
after careful consideration."

01:07:04.729 --> 01:07:09.275
"Only this promotion will be held
at the lowest price."

01:07:11.610 --> 01:07:12.570
[music ends]

01:07:12.653 --> 01:07:14.155
Where's the nutritional information?

01:07:14.238 --> 01:07:15.072
What the hell?

01:07:15.781 --> 01:07:16.907
Where's this from?

01:07:18.034 --> 01:07:20.453
Sir, didn't you say
you couldn't make it today?

01:07:20.536 --> 01:07:24.540
Are you trying to sell
this unverified product to people?

01:07:24.623 --> 01:07:25.541
What?

01:07:25.624 --> 01:07:27.835
Oh.

01:07:27.918 --> 01:07:30.087
I got an offer to promote it,

01:07:30.171 --> 01:07:31.505
but I haven't posted it yet.

01:07:31.589 --> 01:07:33.174
I just took a few pictures.

01:07:35.259 --> 01:07:36.761
-Get out.
-Okay.

01:07:39.555 --> 01:07:40.389
No.

01:07:41.807 --> 01:07:43.350
I want you out of my gym.

01:07:44.685 --> 01:07:46.520
People like you
have no right to be trainers.

01:07:47.146 --> 01:07:47.980
Excuse me?

01:07:48.647 --> 01:07:52.109
You're all show and no substance.
You only care about appearances.

01:07:53.235 --> 01:07:55.696
You've never seen anything through.

01:07:55.780 --> 01:07:57.239
You only hope for good luck.

01:07:59.325 --> 01:08:02.703
Your life is full of nothing but hot air.

01:08:04.455 --> 01:08:05.456
[exhales]

01:08:06.457 --> 01:08:08.292
Isn't that harsh?

01:08:08.375 --> 01:08:09.627
What? Am I wrong?

01:08:09.710 --> 01:08:11.587
You should be helping with sincerity

01:08:11.670 --> 01:08:13.881
and taking responsibility
for someone's health.

01:08:13.964 --> 01:08:17.510
But you slack off on your main job
and only care about making easy money.

01:08:17.593 --> 01:08:19.887
-Mr. Go.
-[Seul-gi] What?

01:08:19.970 --> 01:08:21.764
It's because of punks like you

01:08:23.224 --> 01:08:25.518
that others take our work lightly.

01:08:25.601 --> 01:08:27.978
[exhales] Jeez, this sucks.

01:08:28.062 --> 01:08:30.314
Fine, I'll quit.

01:08:31.023 --> 01:08:32.817
The nerve of lecturing me
with a tiny gym…

01:08:32.900 --> 01:08:34.401
[Seul-gi] You little brat!

01:08:35.319 --> 01:08:36.862
Hey, Dong-jin!

01:08:36.946 --> 01:08:38.197
[knock on door]

01:08:38.280 --> 01:08:39.281
Come in.

01:08:49.667 --> 01:08:50.960
LETTER OF RESIGNATION

01:08:54.421 --> 01:08:55.422
[Seung-hyo exhales]

01:08:55.506 --> 01:08:56.924
Is this your answer?

01:08:57.007 --> 01:08:57.967
No.

01:08:58.843 --> 01:09:00.511
I haven't found the answer yet.

01:09:01.804 --> 01:09:04.473
This is the only way
I can take responsibility.

01:09:10.104 --> 01:09:10.938
[lighter clicks]

01:09:11.021 --> 01:09:12.648
-What?
-[Jeong-min] Mr. Yoon.

01:09:16.902 --> 01:09:18.404
Gosh, this is hot.

01:09:18.487 --> 01:09:20.990
-[everyone clamoring]
-Hey!

01:09:21.824 --> 01:09:26.162
-Can't you act normally?
-I wanted to try something new and cool.

01:09:26.245 --> 01:09:27.913
It wasn't cool at all.

01:09:27.997 --> 01:09:29.915
What if you'd set the sprinklers off?

01:09:29.999 --> 01:09:31.584
[mouthing]

01:09:33.460 --> 01:09:35.796
-We took care of Buryeong-dong.
-What?

01:09:36.589 --> 01:09:39.466
-How?
-We settled with the old man.

01:09:39.550 --> 01:09:41.510
We're going to replace his water pipes.

01:09:42.052 --> 01:09:45.181
Your uptight boss surprisingly
wanted to do it.

01:09:45.264 --> 01:09:47.308
No, that's ridiculous.

01:09:47.391 --> 01:09:48.684
That wasn't our fault.

01:09:48.767 --> 01:09:49.977
You're right.

01:09:50.603 --> 01:09:52.897
I'm not one to compromise
with reality like this.

01:09:54.106 --> 01:09:55.274
But this is my answer.

01:09:57.234 --> 01:09:59.820
And you're a valuable member
of Atelier In.

01:10:00.529 --> 01:10:03.991
For us, you're more important
than the company's profits and losses.

01:10:05.242 --> 01:10:06.243
Mr. Choi.

01:10:06.911 --> 01:10:08.037
[Seung-hyo] So…

01:10:08.120 --> 01:10:10.581
make sure you learn
and grow from this mistake.

01:10:10.664 --> 01:10:14.168
As you make mistakes,
face obstacles, and get scolded here,

01:10:14.835 --> 01:10:17.254
keep looking for your answer.

01:10:17.338 --> 01:10:19.673
Yes, sir. I'll work hard.

01:10:20.716 --> 01:10:21.717
[Jeong-min gasps]

01:10:21.800 --> 01:10:23.552
-Go sit down.
-Yes, sir.

01:10:24.553 --> 01:10:25.763
You're the best.

01:10:26.722 --> 01:10:28.057
You're so cool today too.

01:10:28.140 --> 01:10:29.141
I swear!

01:10:29.225 --> 01:10:31.268
He does all the cool things by himself.

01:10:31.352 --> 01:10:34.188
Hey, you think Seung-hyo
was born a genius?

01:10:34.271 --> 01:10:35.397
Not at all.

01:10:35.481 --> 01:10:37.358
He used to make so many mistakes.

01:10:37.441 --> 01:10:40.110
He's talking from his own experiences
right now.

01:10:40.194 --> 01:10:42.488
-Why would you make that up?
-[Na-yun laughs]

01:10:42.571 --> 01:10:44.031
Doesn't it seem convincing?

01:10:44.615 --> 01:10:45.532
Jeez.

01:10:46.075 --> 01:10:49.286
Did the client give you a hard time?

01:10:49.370 --> 01:10:51.121
Don't get me started.

01:10:51.205 --> 01:10:55.417
If I think about how he grilled me
day and night for three days.

01:10:55.501 --> 01:10:57.294
-Jeez!
-It wasn't Seung-hyo?

01:10:57.378 --> 01:10:58.754
-[Seung-hyo] What?
-Me?

01:10:58.837 --> 01:10:59.755
[Na-yun] Yes.

01:11:00.256 --> 01:11:02.216
I was going to tell you.

01:11:02.800 --> 01:11:04.426
You have bags under your eyes.

01:11:05.386 --> 01:11:08.722
Your cheeks are flushed
and you look feverish.

01:11:08.806 --> 01:11:10.808
Hey, get off.

01:11:10.891 --> 01:11:11.850
[solemn music playing]

01:11:11.934 --> 01:11:12.768
What's going on?

01:11:12.851 --> 01:11:15.187
Are you sick?

01:11:15.271 --> 01:11:17.773
I'm sick? [chuckles nervously]

01:11:17.856 --> 01:11:20.859
I'm completely fine. What are you saying?

01:11:21.402 --> 01:11:22.528
I'm not sick.

01:11:22.611 --> 01:11:23.862
You're being so strange.

01:11:23.946 --> 01:11:24.947
-[Na-yun] Mr. Choi!
-Hey!

01:11:25.030 --> 01:11:26.907
What's wrong? Are you okay?

01:11:26.991 --> 01:11:29.785
What? Yeah.

01:11:30.786 --> 01:11:31.787
[exhales wearily]

01:11:35.624 --> 01:11:36.542
[exhales softly]

01:11:39.920 --> 01:11:40.921
[exhales]

01:11:42.131 --> 01:11:43.007
[groans softly]

01:11:46.802 --> 01:11:47.970
[young Seung-hyo crying] Mom!

01:11:48.554 --> 01:11:50.889
Mom, don't go!

01:11:51.807 --> 01:11:53.684
[crying]

01:11:55.602 --> 01:11:57.313
[continues crying]

01:12:02.151 --> 01:12:03.777
[slow music playing]

01:12:14.079 --> 01:12:16.206
[sniffing]

01:12:16.290 --> 01:12:17.875
Hey, why are you crying?

01:12:17.958 --> 01:12:19.585
Are you still a baby?

01:12:19.668 --> 01:12:21.462
I'm not a baby.

01:12:21.962 --> 01:12:24.882
Your mom's going to work.
You're a baby if you cry like that.

01:12:25.758 --> 01:12:26.800
I'm not crying.

01:12:28.427 --> 01:12:30.387
These are the ddakjis I won yesterday.

01:12:31.221 --> 01:12:32.473
I'll give all of them to you.

01:12:32.973 --> 01:12:35.934
When we play
Red Light, Green Light tomorrow,

01:12:36.018 --> 01:12:37.353
I'll tag you.

01:12:38.145 --> 01:12:39.938
I don't do this for just anyone.

01:12:40.022 --> 01:12:42.107
-Got it?
-It's not good to be tagged.

01:12:43.067 --> 01:12:44.026
[clicks tongue]

01:12:45.027 --> 01:12:48.030
Then, I'll buy you
a Pikachu-shaped pork cutlet.

01:12:49.156 --> 01:12:50.074
Do you have money?

01:12:50.866 --> 01:12:51.700
[clicks tongue]

01:12:52.284 --> 01:12:53.786
Let's just eat tteokbokki.

01:12:53.869 --> 01:12:55.079
We can go to my dad.

01:12:55.662 --> 01:12:56.580
Let's go.

01:13:13.847 --> 01:13:14.932
[weakly] Mom.

01:13:34.660 --> 01:13:35.661
[groans softly]

01:13:46.130 --> 01:13:47.172
Seok-ryu.

01:13:50.217 --> 01:13:51.468
You're really here.

01:13:54.138 --> 01:13:55.973
[chuckles softly] I'm so glad.

01:14:02.020 --> 01:14:03.021
[exhales weakly]

01:14:05.732 --> 01:14:06.692
[exhales weakly]

01:14:08.902 --> 01:14:10.154
[exhales]

01:14:12.197 --> 01:14:13.240
[exhales]

01:14:18.537 --> 01:14:19.621
[music fades]

01:14:24.126 --> 01:14:25.210
Welcome back.

01:14:25.294 --> 01:14:26.712
-Hello.
-[Jae-suk chuckles]

01:14:26.795 --> 01:14:27.629
Hi.

01:14:27.713 --> 01:14:30.132
I'm sure today was sudden. I'm very sorry.

01:14:30.215 --> 01:14:31.758
Was it hard looking after Yeon-du?

01:14:31.842 --> 01:14:34.970
Not at all.

01:14:35.053 --> 01:14:37.598
After dealing with
grown, disgusting kids for so long,

01:14:37.681 --> 01:14:42.102
looking after a baby was so pleasant.
[chuckles]

01:14:42.186 --> 01:14:44.897
-Leave her with us from time to time.
-I appreciate the thought.

01:14:44.980 --> 01:14:46.440
Of course.

01:14:47.024 --> 01:14:48.942
Where is Yeon-du now?

01:14:50.027 --> 01:14:50.861
[knock on door]

01:14:51.820 --> 01:14:52.654
Ms. Jung?

01:14:52.738 --> 01:14:54.615
[shushes, whispering] Be quiet.

01:14:55.449 --> 01:14:56.742
She's sleeping.

01:14:56.825 --> 01:14:59.620
Okay. I have to wake her
and take her home though.

01:14:59.703 --> 01:15:01.413
Wake her later.

01:15:01.914 --> 01:15:04.625
-Let me watch her for a little more.
-Yeah, okay.

01:15:07.377 --> 01:15:08.295
[exclaims]

01:15:15.427 --> 01:15:19.181
No matter how much I see her,
I just want to see her some more.

01:15:19.264 --> 01:15:20.474
[chuckles softly]

01:15:20.557 --> 01:15:23.268
How is she so pretty?

01:15:25.103 --> 01:15:27.272
Her eyes are pretty.

01:15:27.773 --> 01:15:28.857
Her nose is pretty.

01:15:30.025 --> 01:15:31.818
Every part of her is pretty.

01:15:32.945 --> 01:15:37.908
Right? I know she's my daughter,
but she amazes me every time I see her.

01:15:37.991 --> 01:15:39.368
[Mo-eum chuckles softly]

01:15:39.451 --> 01:15:42.371
I wish Yeon-du was my daughter too.

01:15:42.955 --> 01:15:44.331
-Yeah…
-[Mo-eum chuckles softly]

01:15:44.915 --> 01:15:46.792
[amusing music playing]

01:15:46.875 --> 01:15:49.294
-What?
-That's not what I meant.

01:15:49.378 --> 01:15:51.588
I just meant she's so pretty.

01:15:51.672 --> 01:15:53.924
Right. I got it.
I didn't get the wrong idea.

01:15:54.007 --> 01:15:54.925
Okay.

01:16:11.733 --> 01:16:12.776
[music fades]

01:16:17.906 --> 01:16:20.993
[in normal voice] How cute.
You haven't changed at all.

01:16:21.785 --> 01:16:22.953
Excuse me?

01:16:23.036 --> 01:16:24.079
What?

01:16:24.162 --> 01:16:25.539
What did I just say?

01:16:26.290 --> 01:16:27.624
You said I was cute.

01:16:27.708 --> 01:16:31.128
Well, all animals and people
are cute as babies.

01:16:31.211 --> 01:16:33.589
-[chuckles nervously]
-I see. [chuckles nervously]

01:16:33.672 --> 01:16:35.132
That must be Mr. Choi next to you.

01:16:35.215 --> 01:16:37.050
This must be your neighborhood friend.

01:16:37.134 --> 01:16:38.719
The three of you must be very close.

01:16:38.802 --> 01:16:40.012
[Mo-eum] Yes.

01:16:40.095 --> 01:16:41.388
Those two were friends first.

01:16:41.471 --> 01:16:44.683
I started hanging out with them
after I moved here.

01:16:44.766 --> 01:16:46.602
You visit each other's houses often too?

01:16:46.685 --> 01:16:47.853
Yes, of course.

01:16:49.354 --> 01:16:51.565
That reminds me.

01:16:52.065 --> 01:16:55.652
Aside from Seung-hyo,
you're the first man to be in my room.

01:16:58.530 --> 01:16:59.906
Man?

01:16:59.990 --> 01:17:00.991
Goodness.

01:17:01.074 --> 01:17:02.659
[quirky music playing]

01:17:02.743 --> 01:17:04.870
-Why did I say that?
-[exhales softly]

01:17:04.953 --> 01:17:07.414
Well… Come to think of it,
this isn't the first time.

01:17:07.497 --> 01:17:08.457
Ah…

01:17:08.540 --> 01:17:12.127
A technician came in here to fix
the air conditioner when it broke.

01:17:13.045 --> 01:17:14.046
He was a man.

01:17:14.129 --> 01:17:17.716
All of my nephews are boys too.
I must've overlooked them. [chuckles]

01:17:17.799 --> 01:17:18.967
-I see.
-[Mo-eum] Yeah.

01:17:19.593 --> 01:17:21.053
[chuckles nervously]

01:17:23.180 --> 01:17:25.766
[Jae-suk] Mo-eum, come and eat!

01:17:25.849 --> 01:17:29.269
Dan-ho, stay for dinner!

01:17:29.770 --> 01:17:31.772
-Would you like to eat dinner?
-Dinner?

01:17:31.855 --> 01:17:33.482
My mom's a great cook.

01:17:33.565 --> 01:17:35.567
Dinner sounds good. [chuckles nervously]

01:17:36.109 --> 01:17:38.320
-Should I wake Yeon-du first?
-Sure.

01:17:38.403 --> 01:17:39.321
Wake her up.

01:17:40.030 --> 01:17:42.074
[Dan-ho] Yeon-du, wake up.

01:17:42.157 --> 01:17:43.408
[Yeon-du groans softly]

01:17:43.492 --> 01:17:44.493
[Dan-ho] Open your eyes.

01:17:44.576 --> 01:17:46.536
-[Yeon-du groans softly]
-Please.

01:17:48.330 --> 01:17:49.414
[exhales]

01:17:57.798 --> 01:17:58.799
[inhales]

01:18:12.562 --> 01:18:13.563
[grunts softly]

01:18:19.778 --> 01:18:20.987
[soft music playing]

01:18:22.030 --> 01:18:25.325
You asked me how I'm always there to see
your life's embarrassing moments.

01:18:30.455 --> 01:18:32.666
How are you always there when I'm sick?

01:18:47.889 --> 01:18:48.849
[exhales]

01:18:49.933 --> 01:18:50.767
[grunts softly]

01:18:58.358 --> 01:18:59.401
[Seok-ryu] Are you up?

01:19:02.070 --> 01:19:03.447
Are you okay?

01:19:04.156 --> 01:19:05.240
Why are you here?

01:19:07.868 --> 01:19:10.412
-Why would you barge into my room?
-I mean…

01:19:10.495 --> 01:19:14.374
Mr. Yoon said you were really out of it.

01:19:14.458 --> 01:19:18.670
He called to say
you nearly passed out before going home.

01:19:19.713 --> 01:19:21.339
I came and rang the doorbell.

01:19:21.423 --> 01:19:22.799
No one came to the door.

01:19:24.801 --> 01:19:27.721
You could've called me if you were sick.

01:19:27.804 --> 01:19:29.848
Why would you suffer on your own?

01:19:29.931 --> 01:19:31.475
I'm not going to call you anymore.

01:19:32.142 --> 01:19:33.435
Even if something happens,

01:19:34.019 --> 01:19:35.145
whatever the reason,

01:19:36.438 --> 01:19:37.564
it won't happen again.

01:19:40.108 --> 01:19:41.526
So just go.

01:19:41.610 --> 01:19:42.611
Do whatever you want.

01:19:43.820 --> 01:19:46.406
Even if you cut ties with me, eat first.

01:19:47.199 --> 01:19:50.076
Do you have any food in the fridge?
I'll go and check.

01:19:58.168 --> 01:19:59.127
[exhales]

01:20:08.678 --> 01:20:11.932
What do the people in this house eat?

01:20:19.272 --> 01:20:20.649
[Seung-hyo] Seriously?

01:20:31.201 --> 01:20:32.285
What's this?

01:20:32.369 --> 01:20:34.412
[papers rustling]

01:20:48.009 --> 01:20:50.053
DIAGNOSIS

01:20:52.639 --> 01:20:55.433
JUNE 24, 2024
PARTIAL GASTRECTOMY FOR STOMACH CANCER

01:20:56.309 --> 01:20:57.394
[emotional music playing]

01:20:57.477 --> 01:20:59.813
ADMITTED WITH ABDOMINAL PAIN
OUTPATIENT SURGERY

01:21:02.148 --> 01:21:02.983
BAE SEOK-RYU

01:21:03.066 --> 01:21:05.193
Hey, your fridge was totally empty.

01:21:05.277 --> 01:21:07.654
I'll run to my house and get some…

01:21:12.826 --> 01:21:13.994
What is this?

01:21:16.371 --> 01:21:18.540
Hey. This is a mistake, right?

01:21:18.623 --> 01:21:19.875
Why is your name on here?

01:21:19.958 --> 01:21:21.793
I should've gone home first.

01:21:21.877 --> 01:21:23.336
It was a hassle, so I just came up.

01:21:23.420 --> 01:21:25.797
What on earth is this?

01:21:25.881 --> 01:21:28.174
Don't you know? It's a diagnosis.

01:21:29.467 --> 01:21:30.969
I needed it for something.

01:21:32.304 --> 01:21:35.974
I should've taken it that day.
I had to make a second trip there.

01:21:38.768 --> 01:21:39.769
Was this it?

01:21:41.021 --> 01:21:42.063
Is this why you came back?

01:21:44.691 --> 01:21:47.444
[sighs] This is why
I didn't want to tell you.

01:21:50.697 --> 01:21:53.658
[exhales] Hey, I don't care.

01:21:53.742 --> 01:21:57.162
I'll never tell you anyway
even if I tell everyone else in the world.

01:21:59.706 --> 01:22:00.540
Are you sick?

01:22:01.625 --> 01:22:02.667
I was sick.

01:22:04.002 --> 01:22:05.921
-And now?
-I'm okay.

01:22:07.130 --> 01:22:08.340
[sighs softly]

01:22:08.423 --> 01:22:09.424
You…

01:22:09.507 --> 01:22:11.051
[emotional music continues playing]

01:22:11.134 --> 01:22:13.261
How could you not tell me about this?

01:22:14.638 --> 01:22:16.139
Because of this.

01:22:17.724 --> 01:22:19.976
-I was afraid you'd act like this.
-Hey…

01:22:20.852 --> 01:22:23.021
[voice shaking] This is how little
I meant to you?

01:22:24.648 --> 01:22:26.983
Even as a friend,
I meant this little to you?

01:22:27.651 --> 01:22:29.736
You're sick.
I didn't mean to make it worse.

01:22:29.819 --> 01:22:30.654
You should rest.

01:22:30.737 --> 01:22:33.615
[sniffles] I'll ask Mo-eum
to buy you some porridge.

01:22:34.324 --> 01:22:35.283
Get some rest!

01:22:35.367 --> 01:22:36.368
[exhales]

01:22:43.166 --> 01:22:44.000
I have to go home.

01:22:44.709 --> 01:22:45.669
We need to talk.

01:22:45.752 --> 01:22:46.920
Let's talk later.

01:22:47.003 --> 01:22:48.630
How can I wait until later?

01:22:51.758 --> 01:22:52.592
You…

01:22:53.510 --> 01:22:55.053
How could you do this to me?

01:22:56.638 --> 01:22:57.639
Seok-ryu.

01:22:58.807 --> 01:23:01.226
How much longer
were you going to put this off for?

01:23:04.729 --> 01:23:06.606
How long were you going to hide this for?

01:23:07.399 --> 01:23:08.900
Seung-hyo. [inhales]

01:23:09.609 --> 01:23:11.820
[voice shaking] This doesn't make sense!

01:23:13.196 --> 01:23:16.950
How could you go through something
like that without telling anyone?

01:23:20.453 --> 01:23:24.457
Stomach cancer surgery is serious.
How could you not tell anyone?

01:23:25.375 --> 01:23:26.668
[Mi-suk] Who has cancer?

01:23:28.003 --> 01:23:29.004
[door closes]

01:23:29.087 --> 01:23:30.880
[emotional music continues playing]

01:23:31.506 --> 01:23:33.133
[Seok-ryu's breath trembling]

01:23:36.302 --> 01:23:39.264
[Mi-suk] I heard it from outside.
Stomach cancer?

01:23:40.598 --> 01:23:42.017
Who has cancer?

01:23:48.314 --> 01:23:49.691
Who has cancer?

01:24:01.286 --> 01:24:02.120
Is it you?

01:24:09.961 --> 01:24:11.337
Is it really you?

01:24:16.509 --> 01:24:19.137
[whimpering]

01:24:22.682 --> 01:24:25.852
[both crying hysterically]

01:24:33.818 --> 01:24:38.490
[Seok-ryu] To be honest, the first person
I wanted to call was Seung-hyo.

01:24:40.075 --> 01:24:42.243
Just like when I'd fall
and scrape my knee,

01:24:43.286 --> 01:24:45.413
I wanted my mom to hold me as I cried.

01:24:46.956 --> 01:24:51.127
If I had, would it have made the cancer
seems like it was no big deal?

01:24:51.753 --> 01:24:53.797
Could I have brushed it off
and gotten back up?

01:24:54.422 --> 01:24:56.216
[emotional music playing]

01:24:56.299 --> 01:24:57.550
I mean it when I say

01:24:58.927 --> 01:25:00.136
that I really wanted to live.

01:25:01.054 --> 01:25:05.016
DARKNESS IN LIFE

01:25:05.100 --> 01:25:08.895
LIGHT OF LIFE

01:25:08.978 --> 01:25:10.897
[slow pop song playing]

01:25:41.719 --> 01:25:45.932
LOVE NEXT DOOR

01:25:46.891 --> 01:25:49.936
[Seung-hyo] Back then,
I should've run to Seok-ryu.

01:25:50.603 --> 01:25:53.356
She sent all those signals in the dark,

01:25:53.940 --> 01:25:54.983
and I missed them all.

01:25:55.066 --> 01:25:56.109
[Seok-ryu] Mom!

01:25:56.192 --> 01:25:57.360
If their child is sick,

01:25:57.443 --> 01:26:00.029
a parent would go
to the moon or Mars for them.

01:26:00.113 --> 01:26:01.614
[Mo-eum] You said it was okay to cry.

01:26:01.698 --> 01:26:03.324
I'll keep it secret too.

01:26:04.826 --> 01:26:08.413
[Seung-hyo] You hurt
the people who love you.

01:26:09.497 --> 01:26:11.708
[Seok-ryu] You don't know anything!

01:26:11.791 --> 01:26:13.918
You don't know how I feel!

01:26:14.002 --> 01:26:18.089
[Seung-hyo] When things are really tough,
you lean on the people closest to you.

01:26:22.260 --> 01:26:25.263
Subtitle translation by: Sue Mounce
